{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla","id":1458511,"title":"Tzimisce Rule the Camarilla","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-03T07:44:39-07:00","id":1458511,"title":"Tzimisce Rule the Camarilla","content":"This comes from the other thread but I wanted to talk more on this topic and I figured I could bring it to a new thread since it's a discussion about what could be in an alternative setting rather than a discussion canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1458152#post1458152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly the Ventrue are the vanilla option.<br /> <br /> If I was redoing V:TM, I'd ditch the Ventrue and have the Tzimisce as the rulers of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>So CT, how do you think this idea would play out in practice? I'm assuming that these would Old Clan Tzimisce or something akin to them. That would suit me, since I'm a big fan of the OCT. I'm thinking that Tzimisce would be ultraconservative, even more so than the Ventrue, and may well represent the declining power of feudalism, personal ability, honor, land, and old ways of maintaining power as opposed to finance and media, as examples. Should there be a rival in the Camarilla (matching a canon one or something different?) that could represent new money?<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear more detailed thoughts from CTP or anybody else on the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T08:09:51-07:00","id":1458520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla#post1458511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This comes from the other thread but I wanted to talk more on this topic and I figured I could bring it to a new thread since it's a discussion about what could be in an alternative setting rather than a discussion canon.<br /> <br /> So CT, how do you think this idea would play out in practice? I'm assuming that these would Old Clan Tzimisce or something akin to them. That would suit me, since I'm a big fan of the OCT. I'm thinking that Tzimisce would be ultraconservative, even more so than the Ventrue, and may well represent the declining power of feudalism, personal ability, honor, land, and old ways of maintaining power as opposed to finance and media, as examples. Should there be a rival in the Camarilla (matching a canon one or something different?) that could represent new money?<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear more detailed thoughts from CTP or anybody else on the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Tzimisce as a replacement for the Ventrue would have to be changed a bit but would work well as a central conflict within the Camarilla. As you say, it would be interesting to note the Tzimisce as representing Old World money via the power of land and direct domination of ones' vassals via feudalism.<br /> <br /> They would be more directly the kind of vampires that are keeping up the system of Princes, prestige, nobility, Domain, and all of this stuff that groups like the Anarchs hate. They'd have the kind of power to enforce this domination via their Disciplines as well as minions so they don't have to be Old Clan Tzimisce if you go with the 5th Edition Disciplines of giving them Dominate. However, funnily, I think the Tzimisce would actually be very useful to the Camarilla in the Modern Nights with Vicissitude. With the ability to change your face every few decades then the Tzimisce don't necessarily have to worry about photos, identities, and fake personas the way other Clans do. They can even use these as punishments to enforce their power as well.<br /> <br /> If we stick with the &quot;classic&quot; Tzimisce we can also have a rivalry for power with the Tremere and Tzimisce with the two sides uneasily being together as well as constantly jockeying for power. You could perhaps have the Ventrue being the Clan of Merchants but not able to overthrow the Tzimisce due to them being the traditional power structure (an alternative might also be to use the Giovanni instead).<br /> <br /> It certainly makes the Anarch conflict to be more interesting as the Tzimisce show vampire society at its most atavistic and anarchonistic but also powerful and terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T09:13:00-07:00","id":1458528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could perhaps have the Ventrue being the Clan of Merchants but not able to overthrow the Tzimisce due to them being the traditional power structure</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't make sense. The Venture during the Dark Ages were the defacto feudal lords and traditional power structure of Kindred society. But as time progressed and modernity increasingly became the main paradigm, certain portions of the Venture, who focused on more mercantile functions, started to become the new leaders of Kindred society basically. The Venture who wanted to remain in the old ways of feudalism and traditional power structure joined the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Basically what you described in your whole post, scrapping out Tzimisce out the equation for the sake of inference.. is essentially Venture antribu already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T09:16:33-07:00","id":1458529,"title":"","content":"I find the idea of the Tzmisce leading the cam funny, since they're only nominally leaders of the Sabbat, with most of the actual work done by Lasombra and Brujah. The Tzmisce can give a good talk about being a freak, but they're not center stage material in\u200b a normal society. Their disciplies aren't leader disciplines, they're support disciplines. They have more in common with Malks and Gangrel than any of the other Cam clans.<br /> <br /> Joining the Cam? Well, I really like the idea that Vicissitude is richly persecuted, but it could work if you scrapped that, sure. But then you've got the follow on effect of the masquerade being extra easy to patch up if you can just change face. Too easy. Takes a lot of drama out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-03-2021, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T09:32:20-07:00","id":1458534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458528#post1458528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't make sense. The Venture during the Dark Ages were the defacto feudal lords and traditional power structure of Kindred society. But as time progressed and modernity increasingly became the main paradigm, certain portions of the Venture, who focused on more mercantile functions, started to become the new leaders of Kindred society basically. The Venture who wanted to remain in the old ways of feudalism and traditional power structure joined the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Basically what you described in your whole post, scrapping out Tzimisce out the equation for the sake of inference.. is essentially Venture antribu already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we're well off the reservation of switching things around from canon.<br /> <br /> And the Tzimisce have Vicissitude, magic, Ghoul Families, and other things that would allow them to be able to hold their position as Feudal Lords better than the Ventrue Antitribu.<br /> <br /> Also, why I suggested the Giovanni would be better.<br /> <br /> Basically, just kick the Ventrue to the curb completely. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458529#post1458529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the idea of the Tzmisce leading the cam funny, since they're only nominally leaders of the Sabbat, with most of the actual work done by Lasombra and Brujah. The Tzmisce can give a good talk about being a freak, but they're not center stage material in\u200b a normal society. Their disciplies aren't leader disciplines, they're support disciplines. They have more in common with Malks and Gangrel than any of the other Cam clans.<br /> <br /> Joining the Cam? Well, I really like the idea that Vicissitude is richly persecuted, but it could work if you scrapped that, sure. But then you've got the follow on effect of the masquerade being extra easy to patch up if you can just change face. Too easy. Takes a lot of drama out</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's be honest, the Lasombra are in charge because the Tzimisce let them think they are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T09:47:57-07:00","id":1458536,"title":"","content":"In the other thread, people were calling Ventrue boring and \u201cvanilla.\u201d I would argue that Old Clan Tzimisce are just weaker Ventrue. Their Discipline set just doesn\u2019t allow for full scale Sect leadership. Animalism, Auspex and Dominate would be great for ruling smaller retinues for extremely territorial shut-ins who don\u2019t venture too far behind their fiefs. Without the crowd swaying ability of Presence or the survivability of Fortitude \u2014 or the mighty oomph of Potence, if compared to Lasombra \u2014 they would be foolish to try to grab the reigns of the largest conglomeration of vampires. They would arguably be outmatched even by the remaining Brujah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T10:21:24-07:00","id":1458539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458520#post1458520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Tzimisce as a replacement for the Ventrue would have to be changed a bit but would work well as a central conflict within the Camarilla. As you say, it would be interesting to note the Tzimisce as representing Old World money via the power of land and direct domination of ones' vassals via feudalism.<br /> <br /> They would be more directly the kind of vampires that are keeping up the system of Princes, prestige, nobility, Domain, and all of this stuff that groups like the Anarchs hate. They'd have the kind of power to enforce this domination via their Disciplines as well as minions so they don't have to be Old Clan Tzimisce if you go with the 5th Edition Disciplines of giving them Dominate. However, funnily, I think the Tzimisce would actually be very useful to the Camarilla in the Modern Nights with Vicissitude. With the ability to change your face every few decades then the Tzimisce don't necessarily have to worry about photos, identities, and fake personas the way other Clans do. They can even use these as punishments to enforce their power as well.<br /> <br /> If we stick with the &quot;classic&quot; Tzimisce we can also have a rivalry for power with the Tremere and Tzimisce with the two sides uneasily being together as well as constantly jockeying for power. You could perhaps have the Ventrue being the Clan of Merchants but not able to overthrow the Tzimisce due to them being the traditional power structure (an alternative might also be to use the Giovanni instead).<br /> <br /> It certainly makes the Anarch conflict to be more interesting as the Tzimisce show vampire society at its most atavistic and anarchonistic but also powerful and terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're on the same page with the Tzimisce representing old traditional power, landed gentry and the valued associated with them. If that is the case, they still maintain official leadership over the Camarilla through tradition and the respect that they command, to those elders who value those traditions. They have vampire power more than human power.<br /> <br /> If we keep the Ventrue around, making them the merchants would be a great contrast. They could be the rivals of the Tzimisce, representing new money and a more progressive outlook. Ventrue likely have more money and direct influence in the mortal world. The Tzimisce have landed gentry, but the Ventrue have bankers, corporations, stoke brokers, media moguls. At some point in the 19th century, the Ventrue surpassed Tzimisce in terms of wealth, but Tzimisce still have dominance in the Elysiums. The Ventrue would be more egalitarian: people can work their way up, they like people who are good at managing money more than those of noble lineage. The Ventrue would become the center-left of the vampire world, with the Tzimisce as the right.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce contain all sorts of diverse ideas. One way of representing this is go with Revenant families. Because the Tzimisce are in the Camarilla, I would think that they would rely more heavily on Revenants as they wouldn't have the Sabbat objection to ghouls and would have a greater desire for influence over humanity. The Grimaldi could be one of their connections to modern business and finance. The Zantosa could have social skills. Bratovitch could be fighters.<br /> <br /> In the USA, Ventrue dealt a major blow to the Tzimisce with the rise of industry and decline of agrarianism, notably the American Civil War. The plantation system was a vestige of landed nobility and was likely dominated by the Tzimisce, so the South's defeat after the civil war was bad for the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> The leadership of the Tzimisce wouldn't be as dominant as that of the Ventrue in the canon setting.<br /> <br /> If we go with the Tzimisce as the right wing of vampiric politics, and the Ventrue a center-left, I can see the Tremere as siding with the Ventrue. They are a new Clan, another new money Clan, and the Tzimisce would dislike them not only for fighting over Eastern Europe, but also because they would likely see the Tremere as a bunch of caitiff diablerists - which they kind of are. How would the other Clans align here? Would the Brujah still be the Camarilla's far left?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T10:49:31-07:00","id":1458541,"title":"","content":"I love this idea, honestly. In the canon game lines, the Tzimisce have a narrative during the Dark Medieval, when they and the Ventrue are the clashing landed gentry of the East and West, but as MWIS points out they're barely significant in the modern Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Frame the Fiends as the senescent authoritarian Hapsburgs of the modern night, resorting to increasing monstrousness to keep their talons on power, and the Ventrue as the (equally callous) capitalist vampires who adapted to the decline of monarchies and the rise of merchants, and you can assign a niche for each with roots in real world history.<br /> <br /> The persecution of Jaques de Molay by the church and state for having made enough money to make himself an asset forfeiture target is where I'd start the evolution of the Ventrue in this timeline. Make him a martyr celebrated by Ventrue guilds as well as the Masonic groups of the real world. Imagine the impact this would have on Cainite involvement in, say, the American Revolution, which had so many Freemasons in leadership roles that it was a de facto Masonic conspiracy in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 09-03-2021, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T11:30:15-07:00","id":1458549,"title":"","content":"sounds like one of those bad fanfiction concepts were they completly break the setting in every way they can so long as it makes their favorites finally get their deserved position of god emporer of universe because their favorite is just that amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T12:04:46-07:00","id":1458554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458534#post1458534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's be honest, *<b>LIES*</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Of all the clans that don't rule the camarilla that could, my top choices would be Baali and low-key Settites. The corpse-fuckers could be powerful, but nobody likes them enough to let them lead. In the name of fun: The Tzmisce, Ravnos, and Assamites are all clans the Camarilla should wisely actually want to... erm... genocide, and not just because the Tremere have grudges. <br /> <br /> Vicissitude is a very transgressive discipline, the subject of much fear and loathing, and a massive masquerade violation. The OC Tzmisce don't need to be exterminated, but they're not really a good clan for modern nights. The revenant bloodlines turned vampire are fine so long as they don't have Vicissitude. <br /> The Ravnos are a vice-driven menace who are intrinsically drawn to be hostile to the path of humanity, the only path the Camarilla condone. Killing them all is the humane thing to do. <br /> The Assamites view themselves as Judge, Jury and executioner, which is... really frightening if you're in power and corrupt. That, and the part where they don't seem so interested in lifting the Baali curse. Eventually, like cops who need to make up infractions because their department relies on fines for funding, the Assamites will make up infractions so they can diablerize. (also, my book: Quietus is cultivated by consuming poised blood, which means they need to poison people routinely... that's just monsterous) <br /> <br /> Bloodline wise, the Cam should aim to destroy the Gargoyles, blood brothers, Salubri, Nagaraja, meaghar/Kiasyd, anything tied to lilith, HoS, and of course... this is all because these bloodlines are high masquerade risks. They're all few in number, it's not like they're going to put up a good resistance. Might as well do it. <br /> <br /> It's what you've always wanted from the Cam, CT!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T12:18:09-07:00","id":1458556,"title":"","content":"This is how I see the stylistic differences between the Ventrue and Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> The core of the Tzimisce is their territoriality. They are bound to the land. They see themselves as masters of their land, and don't tolerate competitors in their childer or others on their own territory. They only want servants in their territory. Even others of their clan are fit only to be rival lords who can either be enemies or allies depending on the circumstances. It's harder for them to work with others because too often they'll see other clans as interlopers.<br /> <br /> The core of the Ventrue is their collective action as a clan. They cooperate with each other on an ongoing, institutionalized basis. They are much more dynamic and willing to embrace change because that brings opportunity. They are much better working with others because it's only an extension of their existing clan culture.<br /> <br /> If the Tzimisce were inside the Camarilla, they wouldn't rule it. They make poor leaders of others. They would clash too often with others in order to defend their prerogatives. However, they'd be respected for their independence and individual power. They might also have an independent power base as more rural lords inbetween the urban Princedoms and might be seen partially as a second rural clan alongside the Gangrel. In terms of overall power and influence, the Tzimisce would probably be under the Ventrue, Tremere and Toreador, but above the Malkavians (another clan known for its weaker Clan influence overall but with powerful individual members who can be very influential) and more public than the Nosferatu. There'd probably be a significant number of Tzimisce Princes who ruthlessly made their way to the top, but very few Archons as that would put them in a subservient position. The Brujah would likely oppose the Tzimisce even more than they do the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> In a setting where the Tzimisce replace the Ventrue in the Camarilla, I don't think you have a Camarilla honestly. Too much of the Camarilla represents the culture of the Ventrue. I believe that the concept of the Conclave was something that enabled the Camarilla to be created because it provided the basis of reconciliation between the Ventrue and Brujah. To a Ventrue, the Conclave system represents another way to transform individuals into a political body capable of action. To the Brujah, the Conclaves allowed individual expression and power within the Camarilla. I don't see how that becomes part of the Camarilla without the Ventrue, though maybe the Toreador would be able to push it through. And blood bonding of childer would probably be much more common. The Toreador would likely be the de facto leaders of the Camarilla, but the Camarilla as a whole would be much more fractious as rivalry between the Tremere and Tzimisce would be much more open, probably only controlled by keeping those clans in separate territories. The Brujah would likely become much more important, and more of a leadership clan with frequent disputes with the Tzimisce. The Camarilla would probably be run more as a Toreador-Brujah duopoly on top with the Tremere and Tzimisce next, and the other clans below them in terms of overall clan influence and power.<br /> <br /> In short, there'd be a significant number of Tzimisce Princes in the Camarilla, but less power and influence than you might expect because the Tzimisce in general don't know how to share and therefore alienate everyone else who forms coalitions against them. In one measure they'd appear to be very strong, but they would constantly punch underneath their own weight class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T12:27:47-07:00","id":1458558,"title":"","content":"Imagine the Tremere rose up and pissed off the Ventrue instead of the Tzmisce, and then they sided with the Tzmisce (and perhaps nosferatu/Gangrel) against the Ventrue and their allies. <br /> The Tremere would've died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T13:39:09-07:00","id":1458563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458549#post1458549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sounds like one of those bad fanfiction concepts were they completly break the setting in every way they can so long as it makes their favorites finally get their deserved position of god emporer of universe because their favorite is just that amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/teepublic/image/private/s--DhKOw66w--/t_Resized%20Artwork/c_crop,x_10,y_10/c_fit,h_626/c_crop,g_north_west,h_626,w_470,x_0,y_0/g_north_west,u_upload:v1462829015:production:blanks:mtl53ofohwq5goqjo9ke,x_-395,y_-325/b_rgb:eeeeee/c_limit,f_auto,h_630,q_90,w_630/v1560789579/production/designs/5089548_0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I don't know what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458554#post1458554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vicissitude is a very transgressive discipline, the subject of much fear and loathing, and a massive masquerade violation. The OC Tzmisce don't need to be exterminated, but they're not really a good clan for modern nights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a reason Vicissitude has that reputation: Because Sabbat Tzimisce are morons.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is the ultimate Masquerade Discipline. Armed with it, no vampire has to ever worry about being identified as a guy who was alive 100 years ago again. Al Capone is a constant Masquerade breach because he's a famous buy but five minutes alone with a Tzimisce Prince and a Major boon and he'll look like a completely new vampire. Tzimisce are able to infiltrate any new society they want and look like everybody else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458558#post1458558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine the Tremere rose up and pissed off the Ventrue instead of the Tzmisce, and then they sided with the Tzmisce (and perhaps nosferatu/Gangrel) against the Ventrue and their allies.<br /> <br /> The Tremere would've died.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue only &quot;won&quot; because the Tremere weakened the Tzimicse during the Omen War. The Ventrue aren't even the real leaders of the Camarilla. Rafael de Corazon was the founder of the Camarilla and the Toreador were the real heart of things. The Ventrue couldn't even hold Paris for very long and were just a bunch of German petty warlords when the Tremere offered to make them King (with the Torries help).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-03-2021, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T14:04:54-07:00","id":1458566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458549#post1458549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sounds like one of those bad fanfiction concepts were they completly break the setting in every way they can so long as it makes their favorites finally get their deserved position of god emporer of universe because their favorite is just that amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the fun of it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T14:13:48-07:00","id":1458569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458556#post1458556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how I see the stylistic differences between the Ventrue and Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> The core of the Tzimisce is their territoriality. They are bound to the land. They see themselves as masters of their land, and don't tolerate competitors in their childer or others on their own territory. They only want servants in their territory. Even others of their clan are fit only to be rival lords who can either be enemies or allies depending on the circumstances. It's harder for them to work with others because too often they'll see other clans as interlopers.<br /> <br /> The core of the Ventrue is their collective action as a clan. They cooperate with each other on an ongoing, institutionalized basis. They are much more dynamic and willing to embrace change because that brings opportunity. They are much better working with others because it's only an extension of their existing clan culture.<br /> <br /> If the Tzimisce were inside the Camarilla, they wouldn't rule it. They make poor leaders of others. They would clash too often with others in order to defend their prerogatives. However, they'd be respected for their independence and individual power. They might also have an independent power base as more rural lords inbetween the urban Princedoms and might be seen partially as a second rural clan alongside the Gangrel. In terms of overall power and influence, the Tzimisce would probably be under the Ventrue, Tremere and Toreador, but above the Malkavians (another clan known for its weaker Clan influence overall but with powerful individual members who can be very influential) and more public than the Nosferatu. There'd probably be a significant number of Tzimisce Princes who ruthlessly made their way to the top, but very few Archons as that would put them in a subservient position. The Brujah would likely oppose the Tzimisce even more than they do the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> In a setting where the Tzimisce replace the Ventrue in the Camarilla, I don't think you have a Camarilla honestly. Too much of the Camarilla represents the culture of the Ventrue. I believe that the concept of the Conclave was something that enabled the Camarilla to be created because it provided the basis of reconciliation between the Ventrue and Brujah. To a Ventrue, the Conclave system represents another way to transform individuals into a political body capable of action. To the Brujah, the Conclaves allowed individual expression and power within the Camarilla. I don't see how that becomes part of the Camarilla without the Ventrue, though maybe the Toreador would be able to push it through. And blood bonding of childer would probably be much more common.<br /> <br /> The Toreador would likely be the de facto leaders of the Camarilla, but the Camarilla as a whole would be much more fractious as rivalry between the Tremere and Tzimisce would be much more open, probably only controlled by keeping those clans in separate territories. The Brujah would likely become much more important, and more of a leadership clan with frequent disputes with the Tzimisce. The Camarilla would probably be run more as a Toreador-Brujah duopoly on top with the Tremere and Tzimisce next, and the other clans below them in terms of overall clan influence and power.<br /> <br /> In short, there'd be a significant number of Tzimisce Princes in the Camarilla, but less power and influence than you might expect because the Tzimisce in general don't know how to share and therefore alienate everyone else who forms coalitions against them. In one measure they'd appear to be very strong, but they would constantly punch underneath their own weight class.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I think this overstates some issues and understates some others.<br /> <br /> 1. The Ventrue aren't people who rule by consensus, that's the Toreador's thing. The Ventrue domiciles are ruled by feudal overlords and actually INVADED other vampire territories in order to claim more land as part of their whole deal during V:TDA. The Prince of Paris got himself overthrown because he was a tyrannical bastard, Mithras is another example of being a tyrannical bastard, and Hardelstadt the Elder was also a tyrannical bastard. We also saw that Ancient Rome collapsed because the Ventrue couldn't stand the Brujah existing as having their own independent city-state/nation. Really, the Camarilla only works because the Toreador and Tremere softened the Ventrue's inner Blue Blood privilege.<br /> <br /> 2. The Camarilla didn't really change much about vampire society Pre-Convention of Thorns. Vampire domains were ruled by Princes, the Masquerade, and the Rite of Creation/Destruction. At least those dozen or so cities in Europe that had more than a coterie of vampires. The big difference is outside of Paris, Constantinople, and a few other places the number of vampires in a city isn't probably going to be more than a dozen.<br /> <br /> 3. The Tzimisce actually deserve credit as having a Proto-Camarilla before the Camarilla. Long before Thorns, the Tzimisce were an organized body that had a Council of Voivodes that ruled over all of the territory under Clan Tzimisce and made decisions for the health of the group. While of dubious canonicity, the biggest example of their activity would be what they did to the Vukodlak. He was breaking the Masquerade and trying to eat the Antediluvians so they put him in a permanent torpor as a lesson to others. They wouldn't have been able to wage war on the Tremere either if they couldn't join their forces together to fight against them in alliances.<br /> <br /> 4. The Toreador I'd argue ARE the rulers of the Camarilla but they let the Ventrue sit on the throne because the latter take all the heat for being rulers. In a very real way, the Toreadors handle things behind the scenes, avoid being anyone's most hated enemy, and have the Ventrue spill all of the blood necessary to keep people in line while they seem harmless. The Dark Ages: Toreador novel really goes into how much soft power the Toreadors wield while making the Ventrue the people who crack the whip overtly. I could easily see the Tzimsice filling that role.<br /> <br /> 5. The whole &quot;Tzimisce aren't good rulers&quot; thing ignores that there's a huge number of brilliant ones like the Dracon, Vladimir Rustovich, and of course Dracula. Sure, Yorak and Vykos are more insane priests/mad scientists but every clan has nuances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T15:18:14-07:00","id":1458575,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Tremere would have a worse time in the cam with the Tzimisce in power. I think they wouldn't be in the Cam at all.<br /> <br /> From an in-game perspective, the Tremere managed to get their place by offering their magical services to the Ventrue. The Tzimisce don't need that as they have their Kolduns. From an out-game perspective, the Tzimisce is already a clan with a mystic outlook, so it would still make sense for them to have Kolduns or at least other kind of magical support than the Tremere.<br /> <br /> The Tremere and Ventrue could be easily exchanged by the Giovanni as a support on the corporate and criminal worlds where the Tzimisce have less of a hold. They would give the Cam the same areas of influence, but with another dynamic. The Tremere could be relegated to a bloodline, maybe the Salubri remain an Independent clan (keeping some or most of its reputation pre-Tremere, including as arrogant, self-righteous pricks), and the Ventrue could be actually controlling the Sabbat if they keep their cool, or be relegated to their Antitribu cousins.<br /> <br /> Such arrangement would make for a very different beast in the game in general, but may be interesting to run. It isn't the most probable alternate setting, but I do think it is a plausible one with relatively few adjustments.<br /> <br /> But then, it does have its Achilles Heel: it lacks vanilla. I'm not sure how far we can go in a game without vanilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T00:05:59-07:00","id":1458624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458569#post1458569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I think this overstates some issues and understates some others.<br /> <br /> 1. The Ventrue aren't people who rule by consensus, that's the Toreador's thing. The Ventrue domiciles are ruled by feudal overlords and actually INVADED other vampire territories in order to claim more land as part of their whole deal during V:TDA. The Prince of Paris got himself overthrown because he was a tyrannical bastard, Mithras is another example of being a tyrannical bastard, and Hardelstadt the Elder was also a tyrannical bastard. We also saw that Ancient Rome collapsed because the Ventrue couldn't stand the Brujah existing as having their own independent city-state/nation. Really, the Camarilla only works because the Toreador and Tremere softened the Ventrue's inner Blue Blood privilege.<br /> <br /> 2. The Camarilla didn't really change much about vampire society Pre-Convention of Thorns. Vampire domains were ruled by Princes, the Masquerade, and the Rite of Creation/Destruction. At least those dozen or so cities in Europe that had more than a coterie of vampires. The big difference is outside of Paris, Constantinople, and a few other places the number of vampires in a city isn't probably going to be more than a dozen.<br /> <br /> 3. The Tzimisce actually deserve credit as having a Proto-Camarilla before the Camarilla. Long before Thorns, the Tzimisce were an organized body that had a Council of Voivodes that ruled over all of the territory under Clan Tzimisce and made decisions for the health of the group. While of dubious canonicity, the biggest example of their activity would be what they did to the Vukodlak. He was breaking the Masquerade and trying to eat the Antediluvians so they put him in a permanent torpor as a lesson to others. They wouldn't have been able to wage war on the Tremere either if they couldn't join their forces together to fight against them in alliances.<br /> <br /> 4. The Toreador I'd argue ARE the rulers of the Camarilla but they let the Ventrue sit on the throne because the latter take all the heat for being rulers. In a very real way, the Toreadors handle things behind the scenes, avoid being anyone's most hated enemy, and have the Ventrue spill all of the blood necessary to keep people in line while they seem harmless. The Dark Ages: Toreador novel really goes into how much soft power the Toreadors wield while making the Ventrue the people who crack the whip overtly. I could easily see the Tzimsice filling that role.<br /> <br /> 5. The whole &quot;Tzimisce aren't good rulers&quot; thing ignores that there's a huge number of brilliant ones like the Dracon, Vladimir Rustovich, and of course Dracula. Sure, Yorak and Vykos are more insane priests/mad scientists but every clan has nuances.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1- Wrong. The Ventrue rule because they're honourable, organized, charming and generous. The strongest chimp usually isn't the alpha, the Alpha is the chimp that works well with others. The Toreador are charming, but they're far less honourable, far less organized, and far less generous. They even have a reputation for being mean and petty. <s>The Ventrue are Chads, the Toreador are good looking Karens</s> . The Toreador take a lot of prince seats because, well, the Ventrue aren't so good that they always win, and of the remaining clans, the Toreador are more inclined to want to rule and don't scare people half as much as a Brujah or Lasombra. <br /> <br /> 2: What exactly does the Cam do for those smaller cities? <br /> <br /> 3. Poland. See Poland. Poland got wrecked. The Tzmisce would have only had an agreement because they were territorial enough that if a criminal they wanted brought to justice crossed domain lines it would be a massive issue for all parties involved. <br /> <br /> 4: Toreador are more hated than Ventrue. See clan stereotypes sections. The Ventrue at least put up a front of being fair. The Toreador make their attacks personal. As for Toreador making up a lot of Camarilla culture? Well, that's because there's so many of them and they like to be seen. The Malks and the Nosferatu don't like to be seen, the Brujah stay away from court obligations because it's infuriating. The Toreador aren't actually particularly good at anything. They have one mental ability, one social ability, one physical ability, and a weakness that doesn't really drive them to any extreme. More than any other clan they're generalists, not specialists, and it just so happens that the specialists all have better things to do, so the Toreador are the only ones taking up bullshit roles like Harpy or Keeper of Elysium, roles which aren't necessary or which could be given to a ghoul. <br /> The Tzmisce are one of the most specialised clans, they really have better things to do than play nice in elysium. <br /> <br /> 5- Exceptions aren't rules. Your average Tzmisce is an antisocial hobbiest who lives where he won't be disturbed. Yes, he has great manners, but manners are a crutch, and he's mostly using manners as a pretense so that when you offend him he can turn you into one of his experiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T01:57:34-07:00","id":1458629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5- Exceptions aren't rules. Your average Tzmisce is an antisocial hobbiest who lives where he won't be disturbed. Yes, he has great manners, but manners are a crutch, and he's mostly using manners as a pretense so that when you offend him he can turn you into one of his experiments. </div> </div> </div>You got this so totally mixed up... the Metamorphosists are those antisocial hobbiest you describe and they are far from being the average Tzimisce. They may be the coolest thing in VtM but they do not represent your average member of the Clan. This is true of both modern day and dark ages. Back in the dark medieval the average Tzimisce was a feudal overlord with an extensive web of Ghouls, Childer and Revenants at their beck and call, they are the masters of the blood bond for a reason. In the modern day Sabbat the average Tzimisce is more often either the Pack Priest, and thus the spiritual leader of the pack, or ironically one of the more social types leading their network of Ghouls and/or Revenants and thus one of those who help the Sabbat with their influence over the mortals.<br /> <br /> Auspex gives them foresight and is one of the best, if not the best, Discipline for information gathering. And, especially in a secret society of monsters, information is power. While Dominate and Presence make ruling by an iron hand easier they do not their wielders to grow into competent leaders quote on the opposite having these is likely to make you a poorer leader since you start to rely your rule solely on these powers, that is you rule by forcing others to serve and thus breed enemies for yourself. Auspex provodes tools to rise to the position you wish to have and is much more conductive to ruling wisely and with foresight.<br /> <br /> Animalism on the surface this only give one power over the animals of the land, which back in the dark ages does actually enforce the idea that you rule your whole land as even the animals bow down to you. And since you can control the predators in the woods you can keep the villages under more tight control through fear of the wild. But much more importantly, and often forgotten when Animalism is spoken of, it give one power over the Beast within all Vampires. The Ventrue may bend wills of their servants or force them to love them but still can die under their servants claws and fangs should they just momentarily loose themselves to their Beasts. The Ventrue are also slaves to their Beasts where a Tzimisce hold their Beast in thrall and that of others as well. For all their precense Vampires are controlled by their Beasts, it drives their hunger, it makes their society so predatory. The fear of the Beast, and loosing to it, is the driving force behind the whole philosophies of the Kindred, Paths , Roads and yes even Humanity are all just methods of trying to keep the Beast in check. So in a society of predators Animalism can be surprisingly effective.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude, this is made famous through the efforts of the Metamorphosists who are the undeniable masters of the craft and the Szlachta and Vohzd used in open war. Still it, as mentioned, provides a powerful tool even outside those uses. As mentioned it can be a powerful tool used to keep the silence of the blood, it can be wanted ability for a society whose members are so unchanging as the Vampires are. Think about it. They can help you get or loose tattoos, lengthen or change your hair style, give you that shape you have wanted for a hindred years. These are all useful things but require trust and do not help in leadership that is true. Still for a leader this can be a powerful art. It provides you with warriors much more fierce than any other, assassins crafted to a specific look and able to infiltrate anywhere, it is no illusion to be pierced, and it provides both the stick and the carrot for your vampire subjects. Serve well and be revarded beauty beyond compare transgress and be punished with eternal scarring or much worse.<br /> <br /> Ventrue, Toreador and Lasombra all rule like men and are well suited to rule over men where as Tzimisce rule like Vampires and are well suited to rule Vampires. They are masters of the Beast, insightful and informed rules with means to reward or punish the otherwise unchanging beings that Vampires are. Also they are the Clan that can create the most effective armies without sacrificing immortal lives and throwing Vampires into the front lines. This quality alone should be quite a selling point for letting then lead instead of Ventrue who just want to throw other Kindred Clans onto the front lines, which is also why Gangrel finally left Camarilla getting tired of their immortalities being sacrifices so that the Ventrue could sit on their thrones. And this is before we take Kolduns, who are the true masters of the land, into account, but they are the exceptions like the Metamorphosists not your average Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> In summation I feel that on average the Tzimisce are much more suited to rule Vampiric society than most, but they also have a reputation created by the 1-2% that join the ranks of the Metamorphosists rule the minds of many players and st\u2019s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T02:19:30-07:00","id":1458630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458624#post1458624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1- Wrong. The Ventrue rule because they're honourable, organized, charming and generous.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ventrue Honor? That's like saying Brujah pacifist.&quot;<br /> -The Great White Hype paraphrased<br /> <br /> The Ventrue Antitribu care about honor but I am still mostly influenced by First Edition Chicago Ventrue. The Ventrue are a clan of schemers, gladhanding, honorless politicians and businessmen that have no honor whatsoever. It's why the Anitribu exist and why they rock, IMHO, because they're the ones who said, &quot;Screw the money, I have rules.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, even the nicest Ventrue, like Jan Pieterzsoon, will utterly screw you over for a goddamn percentage to quote Ellen Ripley.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2: What exactly does the Cam do for those smaller cities? </div> </div> </div>There was no Camarilla back in the Dark Ages is what I mean. There were only the domains of local vampires maintaining their territory. What I'm saying is that instead of something the Camarilla invented and enforced, the Camarilla mostly formalized a system that was already widely practiced among vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Poland. See Poland. Poland got wrecked. The Tzmisce would have only had an agreement because they were territorial enough that if a criminal they wanted brought to justice crossed domain lines it would be a massive issue for all parties involved. </div> </div> </div>I mean, that is basically the heart of treaties and territorial governance. The Council of Voivodes existed so that they could wage war on foes and deal with criminals that they couldn't do on their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4: Toreador are more hated than Ventrue. See clan stereotypes sections. The Ventrue at least put up a front of being fair. </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, the latter sentence confuses me. The Ventrue do what now? Again, I just think of Lodin as the iconic Ventue or Queen Anne Bowesley. They REVEL in being unfair pricks.<br /> <br /> Mithras doesn't but Mithras is almost an outlier in his own sect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5- Exceptions aren't rules. Your average Tzmisce is an antisocial hobbiest who lives where he won't be disturbed. Yes, he has great manners, but manners are a crutch, and he's mostly using manners as a pretense so that when you offend him he can turn you into one of his experiments. </div> </div> </div>Is that Tzimisce in general or is that Vykos? Because while we have Vykos and Velya the Flayer, we also have Vladimir Rustovich. I fully agree that the Path of Metamorphisis Tzimsice are a bunch of mad scientist flesh sculptors and would-be Cenobites but I suppose it depends on how you perceive the average Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> When I think of the average Tzimisce, I think Wendy Wade.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Wendy_Wade\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Wendy_Wade</a><br /> <br /> Ex-Lawyer, smart, ambitious, and cunning would-be Bishop of Chicago. Which is to say that I fully believe in the mystical flesh-sculpting side of the Clan but I wouldn't ignore the brilliant leader and territorial warlord side. Even then I always felt the Tzimisce were still very important to the sect's leadership. The Sabbat may usually have their pack leaders be Lasombra but their priests were almost always Tzimisce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-04-2021, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T02:25:49-07:00","id":1458631,"title":"","content":"Auspex and Animalism work great as investigative tools. They're probably the best in terms of getting an early-warning from intruders. However, there's a lot of strong competitors for information: Malkavians, Nosferatu, Corpse-fuckers... <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I could argue that Ventrue are really the best information gatherers because they can control so many humans</span>. <br /> The Tzmisce are little-able to defend themselves with their in-clans. They're also poor hunters until they reach the third level of animalism. They've really just got too much against them to be big and important. Modern streets don't have packs of wild animals on them, and modern weapons give people an insane advantage over beasts. <br /> Vicissitude grants them a curious kind of loyalty. But even if we're not talking about metamorphosists (and I wasn't in my earlier post) it still takes time to get good with Vicissitude. Vicissitude is reliant on knowledge (well, depends on edition, could be a skill) and surgery is not a simple thing even if you can move flesh like clay. Not all Tremere go all-in on thaumaturgy but even the ones that don't still invest a lot of time in it. <br /> <br /> Tzmisce make good advisors, but they are low-tier rulers, barely better than nosferatu, worse than Malkavians and Brujah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T02:46:21-07:00","id":1458632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458630#post1458630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I think of the average Tzimisce, I think Wendy Wade.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Wendy_Wade\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Wendy_Wade</a></div> </div> </div> </div> the average tzimisce is a random shovelhead that managed to survive. yeah, gonna call bull on that one cuz that's an exception, not the rule","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T02:56:09-07:00","id":1458634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458632#post1458632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the average tzimisce is a random shovelhead that managed to survive. yeah, gonna call bull on that one cuz that's an exception, not the rule</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a really good question.<br /> <br /> What is the percentage of Shovelheads who Survive (SWS) versus deliberate Embraces among the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> I mean, the Tzimisce I recall for War Parties are like, &quot;Grab any reasonably rich and well-educated looking person.&quot;<br /> <br /> I always assumed the SWS made up like 20% of the Sabbat at most. I.e a decent chunk but far from a majority. This was just a totally me interpretation of the text, though, and I don't think it was ever confirmed one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T02:56:53-07:00","id":1458635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458624#post1458624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Wrong. The Ventrue rule because they're honourable, organized, charming and generous. The strongest chimp usually isn't the alpha, the Alpha is the chimp that works well with others. The Toreador are charming, but they're far less honourable, far less organized, and far less generous. They even have a reputation for being mean and petty. <s>The Ventrue are Chads, the Toreador are good looking Karens</s> . The Toreador take a lot of prince seats because, well, the Ventrue aren't so good that they always win, and of the remaining clans, the Toreador are more inclined to want to rule and don't scare people half as much as a Brujah or Lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be at odds with the writing in V5. The Ventrue rule because they have the most worldly power and a lot of people want to be in proximety to this unimaginable culmintion of power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T03:10:35-07:00","id":1458636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458635#post1458635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to be at odds with the writing in V5. The Ventrue rule because they have the most worldly power and a lot of people want to be in proximety to this unimaginable culmintion of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I like to be at odds with V5, it really isn't. <br /> The Ventrue are the best clan for accumulating wealth and power, and they need to given their weakness. <br /> They're also the best clan for leading vampires because, not only are they good with backgrounds, but also because they simply are desirable people to do business with. The Ventrue more than other clans value stability (because they have herds to protect) so they will try to be friends with as many vampires as possible, that means yes, a lot of vampires enjoy business with the Ventrue. But it also leads them to be honourable, organized, charming... for business reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T03:18:25-07:00","id":1458637,"title":"","content":"I think we just have to agree to disagree. First of all, yes Malkavians are good for information if you can trust information coming from a madman that just might have hallucinated the whole thing. Nosferatu on the other hand are trustworthy providers of information but that information is gonna cost you, and they are not of your blood and thus can you really rely on them (well the Ventrue need to since they aren\u2019t that good at this), the Giovanni do hold a lot of information, enough so to avoid getting into a war with anyone and staying independent despite basically destroying a High Clan, but they are independent and not involved with the Camarilla. So would you really go to them for your sensitive information? And like the Nosferatu they will have a prise Tag attached. The Tzimisce have these things in-Clan.<br /> <br /> Ventrue can control humans, yes. But that is by stripping them of their will. Also humans are poor spies when it comes to Vampire affairs. Animalism creates useful spies, and yes so can Dominate, but the key here is Auspex that allows for all sorts of information gathering, from objects, from people, by astral projection and when you get to high levels...<br /> <br /> Tzimisce are little-able to defend themselves? How did you come to that conclusion? Or that they are poor hunters? Animalism 2 allows you to call food to you. 3 allows humans to be helpless yes but that is not required. But seriously, any vampire that relies on Disciplines to hunt is a poor vampire indeed and it\u2019s sire should be ashamed of their childe and consider introducing it to the dawn.<br /> <br /> Modern weapons are effective yes, but there is a reason police use dogs you know. Not only to keep people safe from getting potentially shot but also because very very few can remain Clan and take that shot against an attacking dog, we have a sort of primal fear that kicks in when a predator attacks. Let alone if that dog would be enhanced by a few changes. And while the Tzimisce do not have Fortitude they can make use of Vicissitude to protect themselves, besides like said Tzimisce tend to use Ghouls for war not walk into the fire themselves. And to be frank Fortitude is barely useful untill you get into the 3-4+ range. Also it seems they are rather good at surviving considering their homelands is a Shadow Lord territory and the Tzimisce thrived there. <br /> <br /> Also outside of the USA modern weapons are not something found on the street that often, dogs on the other hand are quite common, as are cats and birds. Have you ever been attacked by an angry bird? That is really scary and most definately distracting, you really can\u2019t focus on aming your gun, even less so if it is an entire flock or murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T03:33:25-07:00","id":1458640,"title":"","content":"let me ask y'all a serious question for a bit: what is it a ruler actually does? what does ruling actually require one to do to see their commands enacted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T03:58:11-07:00","id":1458642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458640#post1458640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">let me ask y'all a serious question for a bit: what is it a ruler actually does? what does ruling actually require one to do to see their commands enacted?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in vampire society, it's a matter of scaring, bribing, or persuading the subjects to go along with your decisions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458637#post1458637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we just have to agree to disagree. First of all, yes Malkavians are good for information if you can trust information coming from a madman that just might have hallucinated the whole thing. Nosferatu on the other hand are trustworthy providers of information but that information is gonna cost you, and they are not of your blood and thus can you really rely on them (well the Ventrue need to since they aren\u2019t that good at this), the Giovanni do hold a lot of information, enough so to avoid getting into a war with anyone and staying independent despite basically destroying a High Clan, but they are independent and not involved with the Camarilla. So would you really go to them for your sensitive information? And like the Nosferatu they will have a prise Tag attached. The Tzimisce have these things in-Clan.<br /> <br /> Ventrue can control humans, yes. But that is by stripping them of their will. Also humans are poor spies when it comes to Vampire affairs. Animalism creates useful spies, and yes so can Dominate, but the key here is Auspex that allows for all sorts of information gathering, from objects, from people, by astral projection and when you get to high levels...<br /> <br /> Tzimisce are little-able to defend themselves? How did you come to that conclusion? Or that they are poor hunters? Animalism 2 allows you to call food to you. 3 allows humans to be helpless yes but that is not required. But seriously, any vampire that relies on Disciplines to hunt is a poor vampire indeed and it\u2019s sire should be ashamed of their childe and consider introducing it to the dawn.<br /> <br /> Modern weapons are effective yes, but there is a reason police use dogs you know. Not only to keep people safe from getting potentially shot but also because very very few can remain Clan and take that shot against an attacking dog, we have a sort of primal fear that kicks in when a predator attacks. Let alone if that dog would be enhanced by a few changes. And while the Tzimisce do not have Fortitude they can make use of Vicissitude to protect themselves, besides like said Tzimisce tend to use Ghouls for war not walk into the fire themselves. And to be frank Fortitude is barely useful untill you get into the 3-4+ range. Also it seems they are rather good at surviving considering their homelands is a Shadow Lord territory and the Tzimisce thrived there.<br /> <br /> Also outside of the USA modern weapons are not something found on the street that often, dogs on the other hand are quite common, as are cats and birds. Have you ever been attacked by an angry bird? That is really scary and most definately distracting, you really can\u2019t focus on aming your gun, even less so if it is an entire flock or murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree here.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce are quite good at what they do. Tzimicse ruled domains may be terrorized, run-down, and full of vermin but they are not FAILED domains. Tzimisce know how to rule. Whether it's scaring the shit out of people, blood bonding them, or forcing them into compliance.<br /> <br /> They are the co-rulers of the Sabbat for a reason and that is a greatly disorderly bunch of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-04-2021, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T04:19:43-07:00","id":1458644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458636#post1458636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I like to be at odds with V5, it really isn't.<br /> The Ventrue are the best clan for accumulating wealth and power, and they need to given their weakness.<br /> They're also the best clan for leading vampires because, not only are they good with backgrounds, but also because they simply are desirable people to do business with. The Ventrue more than other clans value stability (because they have herds to protect) so they will try to be friends with as many vampires as possible, that means yes, a lot of vampires enjoy business with the Ventrue. But it also leads them to be honourable, organized, charming... for business reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no way reading the parts in Core, Camarilla and the Companion and come away thinking that Ventrue are &quot;honourable, generous&quot; and &quot;will try to be friends with as many vampires as possible&quot;. And the letter of Victoria Ash shows that the unmoral side of Ventrue isn't just meta knowledge, but is known to vampires that aren't new to the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T04:24:09-07:00","id":1458645,"title":"","content":"For one, my impression in general for the shovelheads is that Lasombra and Tzimisce actually create less of them than other clans that joined the Sabbat, and probably the majority of them are Panders. But yeah, in the not-so-low echelons of the sect my impression is that SWS are at most about 20% of it.<br /> <br /> After all, the instant you get to clan descriptions they are all almost as irked by the prospect of Embracing random people for one-night-stand as any Cam clan.<br /> <br /> On a second point, I'm personally tired of this pointless fight about the Ventrue being capable leaders or not. Both sides have biased but equally valid interpretations of the clans as written and both are becoming quite annoying in their arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T05:01:32-07:00","id":1458650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458644#post1458644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no way reading the parts in Core, Camarilla and the Companion and come away thinking that Ventrue are &quot;honourable, generous&quot; and &quot;will try to be friends with as many vampires as possible&quot;. And the letter of Victoria Ash shows that the unmoral side of Ventrue isn't just meta knowledge, but is known to vampires that aren't new to the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was the Toreador's thing. Clans think they're weak and bitchy/smug but harmless. However, they seem to be everyone's friend if you meet them because they ooze charisma.<br /> <br /> Ventrue don't need friends. They have minions, bosses, and allies.<br /> <br /> Friends?<br /> <br /> I think most Ventrue find that to be optional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458645#post1458645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one, my impression in general for the shovelheads is that Lasombra and Tzimisce actually create less of them than other clans that joined the Sabbat, and probably the majority of them are Panders. But yeah, in the not-so-low echelons of the sect my impression is that SWS are at most about 20% of it.<br /> <br /> After all, the instant you get to clan descriptions they are all almost as irked by the prospect of Embracing random people for one-night-stand as any Cam clan.<br /> On a second point, I'm personally tired of this pointless fight about the Ventrue being capable leaders or not. Both sides have biased but equally valid interpretations of the clans as written and both are becoming quite annoying in their arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to think that it depends greatly on the Ventrue themselves and also, more importantly, the Storyteller. Most Storytellers aren't going to be telling a story about every Ventrue in the WorldTM so it's really whatever Ventrue they have in their Chronicles who can range from smug snakes like La Croix to badass warriors like Jurgen.<br /> <br /> The ST is always right and much of the setting is up to interpretation, which I sometimes forget myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-04-2021, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T05:02:05-07:00","id":1458651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458644#post1458644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no way reading the parts in Core, Camarilla and the Companion and come away thinking that Ventrue are &quot;honourable, generous&quot; and &quot;will try to be friends with as many vampires as possible&quot;. And the letter of Victoria Ash shows that the unmoral side of Ventrue isn't just meta knowledge, but is known to vampires that aren't new to the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've just read V5 right? <br /> Well, Dogging V5 too much is a bannable offense, but to put it nicely, V5 omits a lot of the nuances of many clans. It simplifies clans and, plainly, it does so according to the writer's biases. Ventrue epitomize Conservative Elites, they're old-money. Because the writers in V5 don't like conservative elites, which isn't really a problem, but they don't distance themselves enough from their own work so you really only get the negatives about the Ventrue: They're rich, they're snobbish, people only like them because they got money, they like to sit on thrones and talk down to poor folk, they only use Presence to sow fear into the hearts of subordinates, and <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">they only embrace men because all members need a mustashe to twirl</span></span></span>. it's a caricature that doesn't really take into account the realities of Ventrue living: Ventrue are often acutely vulnerable due to short food supply. They can't just pack up and leave when things go bad without ample preperation. Also, if you've got all the wealth and nobody really likes you, you really become an attractive target. The Ventrue actually have a smaller background advantage in V5 because of the Dominate nerfs (and the lighter weakness doesn't push them so hard) so they can't really be dicks just because they're &quot;powerful&quot;.<br /> <br /> (I'm aware i'm exaggerating a little with how evil they make the Ventrue. They also make the Brujah twice as heroic, the Tzmisce 1000% more organized, The Ravnos actually likeable because they think &quot;trickster&quot; means dashing rogue, and other flanderizations...) <br /> What V5 has done with the Camarilla is more telling. Since the Anarchs are champions of Liberalization and the Camarilla are thus the conservatives, the Cam went from inclusive to exclusive, from secular to religious, and from modern to ludite. The Ventrue, as Paragons of the Camarilla, suffer as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T05:06:23-07:00","id":1458653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458651#post1458651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've just read V5 right?<br /> Well, Dogging V5 too much is a bannable offense, but to put it nicely, V5 omits a lot of the nuances of many clans. It simplifies clans and, plainly, it does so according to the writer's biases. Ventrue epitomize Conservative Elites, they're old-money. Because the writers in V5 don't like conservative elites, which isn't really a problem, but they don't distance themselves enough from their own work so you really only get the negatives about the Ventrue: They're rich, they're snobbish, people only like them because they got money, they like to sit on thrones and talk down to poor folk, they only use Presence to sow fear into the hearts of subordinates, and <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">they only embrace men because all members need a mustashe to twirl</span></span></span>. it's a caricature that doesn't really take into account the realities of Ventrue living: Ventrue are often acutely vulnerable due to short food supply. They can't just pack up and leave when things go bad without ample preperation. Also, if you've got all the wealth and nobody really likes you, you really become an attractive target. The Ventrue actually have a smaller background advantage in V5 because of the Dominate nerfs (and the lighter weakness doesn't push them so hard) so they can't really be dicks just because they're &quot;powerful&quot;.<br /> <br /> (I'm aware i'm exaggerating a little with how evil they make the Ventrue. They also make the Brujah twice as heroic, the Tzmisce 1000% more organized, The Ravnos actually likeable because they think &quot;trickster&quot; means dashing rogue, and other flanderizations...)<br /> What V5 has done with the Camarilla is more telling. Since the Anarchs are champions of Liberalization and the Camarilla are thus the conservatives, the Cam went from inclusive to exclusive, from secular to religious, and from modern to ludite. The Ventrue, as Paragons of the Camarilla, suffer as a result.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually gets into a funny fact that vampires are probably more personalized than players and Storytellers probably think. We mentioned that we shouldn't use NPCs as an example of how a Clan should operate but there's about 2000 vampires of each Clan, give or take a few hundred, so that with 25+ years of vampire supplements, we actually have a pretty large chunk of each clan's membership in our books.<br /> <br /> Lodin isn't the be end all of Ventrue, certainly, anymore than Jurgen is.<br /> <br /> However, both of them in-universe MADE the stereotypes that define the Clans as the entirety of vampiredom could fit in one mid-sized city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-04-2021, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T05:30:21-07:00","id":1458655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458642#post1458642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think in vampire society, it's a matter of scaring, bribing, or persuading the subjects to go along with your decisions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>so close, yet so far.<br /> <br /> the job of a ruler is to distribute the resources they have access too in such a manner that key supporters remain loyal to you. (key supporters don't have to be an individual, it can be a group of ppl) this can be appllied to any position of power (meaning that a key supporter is in itself as possition of power are required to ensure loyalty of his own key supporters) what differs is who are the key supporters (and how many there are in the first place) and what are the resources they can redistribute to ensure loyalty (doesn't need to be material goods, it could also be services or anyhing really). that sounds simple but it get's complicated because who are the key supporters you need are constantly changing and how to ensure the loyalty of one key supporter might loose you another one, etc. etc. but the basics stay the same<br /> <br /> the clan who understand this process the best are the ventrue<br /> <br /> the tzimisce on the other hand regularly fail at this because either they don't recognize key supporters (these are usually their human key supporters or somebody they have a bit of a grude against) or their methodes of ensuring loyalty just don't work (at least not anymore). because of this a tzimisce is regularly fine in smaller positions of power (because they have less key supporters to worry about and they tend to be less demanding) or in positions within the sabbath (because their methodes of ensuring loyalty still work in specific hierarchies, there's basically just nothing left with any significant power outside of the sabbath but at the same time this hierarchy that enables the tzimisce is one of the reasons the sabbath is failing)<br /> <br /> on an unrelated noti find it hilarious that most ppl here defending the tzimisce clearly fail to understand the exact same thing the tzimisce failed to understand which caused their downfall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T05:53:57-07:00","id":1458659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458655#post1458655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tzimisce on the other hand regularly fail at this because either they don't recognize key supporters (these are usually their human key supporters or somebody they have a bit of a grude against) or their methodes of ensuring loyalty just don't work (at least not anymore). because of this a tzimisce is regularly fine in smaller positions of power (because they have less key supporters to worry about and they tend to be less demanding) or in positions within the sabbath (because their methodes of ensuring loyalty still work in specific hierarchies, there's basically just nothing left with any significant power outside of the sabbath but at the same time this hierarchy that enables the tzimisce is one of the reasons the sabbath is failing)<br /> <br /> on an unrelated noti find it hilarious that most ppl here defending the tzimisce clearly fail to understand the exact same thing the tzimisce failed to understand which caused their downfall.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is the Tzimisce aren't exactly &quot;fallen&quot; are they? Being co-rulers of the 2nd most powerful sect in the setting isn't exactly &quot;fallen.&quot; Even with all of the hits the Sabbat have taken due to the Second Inquisition, Camarilla, and Anarchs--they've actually probably had more success in destroying Camarilla Elders in the Gehenna War than they have had in the previous 600 years. After all, now the Elders are on the field and getting exterminated.<br /> <br /> I fully expect them to emerge from the Gehenna War as winners, rather than losers, Mexico and Montreal losses aside.<br /> <br /> The Old Clan Tzimisce are also powerful Elders in both the True Hand and Inconnu, which means that while they may only a handful of vampires, they still wield some of the greatest power in creation.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the biggest benefit of the Tzimisce is going to be the fact that we're going to find out that they're probably majorly positioned across Asia. I fully expect them to be one of the Clans they just to replace the Kuei-Jin with.<br /> <br /> But that's COMPLETELY guesswork on my part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T06:00:28-07:00","id":1458661,"title":"","content":"I don't see it. They don't care enough about poltics or kindred as a whole. If they did rule the Camarilla, they'd probably depend on intermediates to do most of the work that governance and arbitration entail. And what's to stop those kindred from overthrowing them?<br /> <br /> At best, they could be members of the Camarilla who demand sovereignty in their own domains, even when they already have it. They'd use it to prevent other kindred from bothering them and the Traditions to defend the privileges of their elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T06:03:10-07:00","id":1458662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458659#post1458659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is the Tzimisce aren't exactly &quot;fallen&quot; are they? Being co-rulers of the 2nd most powerful sect in the setting isn't exactly &quot;fallen.&quot; Even with all of the hits the Sabbat have taken due to the Second Inquisition, Camarilla, and Anarchs--they've actually probably had more success in destroying Camarilla Elders in the Gehenna War than they have had in the previous 600 years. After all, now the Elders are on the field and getting exterminated.<br /> <br /> I fully expect them to emerge from the Gehenna War as winners, rather than losers, Mexico and Montreal losses aside.<br /> <br /> The Old Clan Tzimisce are also powerful Elders in both the True Hand and Inconnu, which means that while they may only a handful of vampires, they still wield some of the greatest power in creation.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the biggest benefit of the Tzimisce is going to be the fact that we're going to find out that they're probably majorly positioned across Asia. I fully expect them to be one of the Clans they just to replace the Kuei-Jin with.<br /> <br /> But that's COMPLETELY guesswork on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>i forgot for a second we were discussing bad fan fic writing. toreador will win because they've got the better looking asses","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T06:06:37-07:00","id":1458663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458662#post1458662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i forgot for a second we were discussing bad fan fic writing. toreador will win because they've got the better looking asses</div> </div> </div> </div>I do admit I fully believe the Camarilla is the Toreador's baby not the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> I also believe that they created the Camarilla fully because they hated tha