1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T07:52:32-07:00","id":1458679,"title":"","content":"In the canon, the Toreador and Tzimisce don\u2019t rule their respective sects, but they are the heart of each sect. The culture of the Camarilla is largely a result of the Toreador - the desire to be more human, the importance on status and appearances, the facade of beauty with rottenness beneath - it\u2019s the Toreador Clan. The same could be said for the Tzimisce and the Sabbat. The rituals, the over the top cruelty and vampiric supremacy, the weird mysticism, even the Vaulderie was created by the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Of course, in this scenario it may be different, as this is more the Old Clan Tzimisce than the ones who gave the Sabbat it\u2019s character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458662#post1458662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i forgot for a second we were discussing bad fan fic writing. toreador will win because they've got the better looking asses</div> </div> </div> </div>If you hate this idea so much, you don\u2019t have to be in the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T08:19:18-07:00","id":1458680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458679#post1458679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you hate this idea so much, you don\u2019t have to be in the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i wasn't even refering to the tzimisce in charge of the cam thing. i was refering to old clan and the beckoning","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T11:59:54-07:00","id":1458705,"title":"","content":"The problem of citing the Tzimisce Voivodate as some exemplar of the efficacy or strength of Tzimisce rule is that it was something of a disaster in pursuing its goals or even maintaining regular cohesion by the time of the War of Princes certainly. The Dark Ages Tzimisce had massive issues with being hobbled by their sheer overwhelming pride and territoriality.<br /> <br /> Vladimir Rustovich, the Voivode of Voivodes was undermined and betrayed by his own broodmates despite being the head of the whole thing and the guy in charge of their war efforts, such that he would ultimately abandon said efforts to seek revenge on his own brood specifically and the Shadow Lords generally. An explicitly noted problem for the clan in their wars with both the Ventrue and Tremere, and a regular cause of losses within it, was that getting the clan to actually work together was a nightmarish process, where many Tzimisce would refuse to participate in unified efforts/subordinate themselves to another member of their clan/abandon whatever vendetta they might have with another member of their clan, or recognize any problem that didn't threaten their direct territory. It was a massive achievement of leadership that Rustovich could get his clan to work together, just at all. And then his own clanmates ultimately brutally, short sightedly sabotaged him despite the sheer damage that would cause to their war effort. Tzimisce pride and jealousy is a hell of a drug, to paraphrase something.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons the Tremere survived the Tzimisce's attempt to wipe them out, the clan's inability to fully get their act together due to the territorial mindset and vengeful pride that ran rampant within it. The modern clan (pre V5 obviously) has less of a complex in that sense, but the tradeoff there is the shift in overall clan culture has taken it far away from concepts like asserting leadership or cohesion to more of a focus on warped matters of spirit (there's a reason a huge proportion of pack priests, but not ducti, are/were Tzimisce)<br /> <br /> Ironically and at least to their credit, the old pride and territoriality of the Tzimisce was actually useful as far as keeping them out of the clutches of forces like the infernal (who were otherwise the strongest they would ever be as a corrupting force in the medieval era, overall), because the usual pitch of demons/infernal vampires/that kind of thing about being able to offer aid or power would crash hard into a Tzimisce reacting with grave, violent, murderous offense to the clearly insulting suggestion that they needed help from someone else.<br /> <br /> But otherwise? The Voivodate spent most of its time as a loosely organized institution with certainly individually very strong leaders, and a highly marked problem when they came together to do things like wage war as far as tripping over each other's egos and starting up a whole bunch of new internal vendettas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 09-04-2021, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T21:51:00-07:00","id":1459096,"title":"","content":"So let me get back to the original idea a bit with a few of my musings about what this might look like if the Tzimisce lead, or at least were a prominent Clan, in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s go with the Anarch Revolt happening in much the same way as the canon timeline, but the Tzimisce leaders defeat their childer and maintain control over their ancestral domains and are able to unite the Clans to create the Camarilla. They become the most respected founding Clan and their intense interest in feudalism and the honorable aristocratic values informs the Camarilla system. The Ventrue participate as well, as reluctant allies and eventual rivals to the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> As time goes by, the Tzimisce loses power and wealth relative to the Ventrue and the Toreador, as mortal wealth becomes less based on nobles and land and more based on business. Ventrue are new money, Tzimisce old money, and this distinction in part defines the power struggle within the Camarilla. The Ventrue are more egalitarian in a sense, as they believe in upward mobility of those who have the ability to make money or influence people. Alternatively, they don\u2019t believe in noblesse oblige. Ventrue supported central banks, stock investments, big corporations and trading companies, big markets and merchants, democracy, media corporations. The Tzimisce favor landed gentry, slavery, local politics, nationalistic/ethnic/cultural interests. The Ventrue are winning, as we can see.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce rely more heavily on the Revenant families in this setting. The Grimaldi are one of their connections to the modern business world, they also represent a large centralized organization that transcends feudal ideas of territory. The family goes beyond the land. The Zantosa also have a lot of wealth, both ancestral nobility wealth and contacts to the criminal underworld and the world of big vice. The Obertus are mystics and the Bratovitch are warriors along with the Vlaszy who are still alive in this timeline. These Revenant families provide a lot of diverse abilities and resources that keep the Tzimisce Clan from being entirely surpassed by the Ventrue. I\u2019d even go far as to say that a high percentage of Tzimisce vampires come from one of these families and the Revenant family structures bind the Clan across domains that would otherwise have been isolated. <br /> <br /> What about other Clans in this setting? The Ventrue, as said, are the primary rivals of the Tzimisce. They are in some ways like canon, but a bit more ruthless and less honorable, maybe even more supportive of Anarchs or similar movements, as the Tzimisce support absolute rule of the elders. <br /> <br /> The Toreador exist and are also one of the more powerful Clans in the Camarilla, perhaps having a more modern power base than the Tzimisce and favoring policies of the Ventrue over those of the Tzimisce. The Gangrel and Nosferatu are both in the Clan and they have a traditionally more friendly relationship with the Tzimisce. Those two Clans lend their strength to the Tzimisce more so than they supported the Ventrue in canon and their support helps the Tzimisce maintain power. The Nosferatu help provide the Tzimisce with information about their enemies and the modern world. The Gangrel lend their strength to help as well, perhaps given command of wilderness territories by the Tzimisce, making the Gangrel feudal lords over their own rural domains. Malkavians are probably wild cards in this setting, much as they are in canon. <br /> <br /> Can the Tremere be in a Camarilla lead by the Tzimisce? Who knows, but it might be interesting and appropriate if they aren\u2019t. They Tremere could be seen as diablerists and caitiff by the Tzimisce and Camarilla leaders and they are opposed by the Camarilla, so they join the Sabbat. It makes sense considering their rise to power. <br /> <br /> Let\u2019s throw in another change. The more egalitarian Brujah won\u2019t compromise with the new Camarilla ruled by the Tzimisce, who think that the youth should be obedient to the elders and even the more liberal factions are represented by the Ventrue. The Brujah stay with the Sabbat. While we\u2019re at it, let\u2019s have the elder Lasombra defeat their rebellious childer as well and they will join with the Camarilla as well.<br /> <br /> So we have the Camarilla:<br /> Tzimisce<br /> Ventrue<br /> Malkavian<br /> Lasombra<br /> Toreador<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Gangrel<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat:<br /> Brujah<br /> Tremere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T11:41:16-07:00","id":1459164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1458655#post1458655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on an unrelated noti find it hilarious that most ppl here defending the tzimisce clearly fail to understand the exact same thing the tzimisce failed to understand which caused their downfall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you fail to understand that leadership and politics are complex, and so people may have different perceptions from yours without being necessarily more or less informed or accurate. Were it so simple we would lived in a far different world IRL.<br /> <br /> My personal impression, first making it clear that arguments on both sides aren't equal either, is that you abide to a too restrict view of what leadership is. You're taking the Ventrue style and goals as the only standard to measure everything and everyone, and then it is obvious that the Tzimisce won't make it. But there are other forms of leadership and rule. You also have an extremely narrow view of the Tzimisce and who they can be, and refuses to accept that other interpretations are possible with the information we get from the books.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce are the archetypal aristocrats of Europe, especially eastern Europe. They rule through personal ties, family lines, ritual and tradition. And they recognize their key supporters very well, the difference is who their supporters are and how they operate. Traditional aristocrats don't rule through influence over institutions, they rule through influence over people and personal obligation. Extending tendrils over vast distances isn't their style, either, instead strengthening their control over their direct possessions and vassals. Finally, they delegate <i>a lot</i>, relying on others having the direct power as long as they can assure a reasonable degree of loyalty. You can take a look at aristocratic politics even now in Europe and you'll see that the way they do things is really diverse from the way common politicians do.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a Tzimisce led Camarilla would be different from a Ventrue led Camarilla, because they understand and exert power in vastly different ways. The other clans would probably have a far more direct role in controlling mortal institutions because the Tzimisce would expect that instead of seeing them as rivals. They would have more interest in keeping ties to the princes of other cities instead of wanting those princes to be Tzimisce, as long as those Princes follow their traditions. Probably the Traditions of the Camarilla would be a little different, or at least more defined, and there would be guides on proper etiquette for formal meetings.<br /> <br /> And yes, they would have less global power. Global power isn't their thing. Again, this isn't about saying that a Camarilla &quot;ruled&quot; by the Tzimisce would have a ruler as present in everyday affairs as the Ventrue are. Instead it would make itself more present in values like personal loyalty (tempered by the personal hate they frequently have toward the same people) and hospitality, and generally a more archaic aesthetics in the structure. Domains with a proper Tzimisce prince would be less common than domains with a Ventrue Prince in the official setting, and probably with a more structured hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that it wouldn't be the followers of the Path of Metamorphosis. As every clan the Tzimisce isn't a monolith where everyone have the same personality and it wouldn't be the same people creating this structure. Camarilla Tzimisce would be the elders and followers of the old traditions of the clan, not the upstarts that created the Sabbat, Viscissitude or not. Also the Revenant families would have a profound impact, as they would be the primary supporters of Tzimisce influence, and they have a lot of the abilities the clan lacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459096#post1459096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we have the Camarilla:<br /> Tzimisce<br /> Ventrue<br /> Malkavian<br /> Lasombra<br /> Toreador<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Gangrel<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat:<br /> Brujah<br /> Tremere</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting take of it, although not the one I would/will make.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Tremere wouldn't make it to the Camarilla, but that would have other consequences. Not only they have a bad history with the Tzimisce, they also have nothing to offer them. They got where they are by leveraging their mystic services to the Ventrue, but the Tzimisce have their own Kolduns for this. If Tzimisce got into the position to lead the Camarilla, then to me they increased their reliance on Kolduns to stave off Tremere-buffed Ventrue. It is even possible that the standard modern Tzimisce would have Koldunic Sorcery instead of Viscissitude or Dominate (making it mechanically equivalent to Tremere).<br /> <br /> But that would also mean the Ventrue would not only be at a worse shape at the time, they would have a valuable asset in the Tremere. My bet is that this alliance wouldn't get weaker, but stronger, despite the Tremere also not getting as easier a time. They could throw their lot with the Anarch Revolt that already vows for the hunting and destruction of elders, with Ventrue elders being content in commanding things from afar, hidden. The Lasombra would have to contend with Ventrue for influence in the new sect, and maybe didn't stayed for long, or could even have a schism.<br /> <br /> With such developments the times would be a little safer on the vampiric side for the nascent Camarilla, and as many others I see no reason for the Giovanni to not want a part in it. They would bring the mercantile connections the sect would lack without the Ventrue, along with a fair domain over Dominate, and compound their Necromancy with Tzimisce Koldunic Sorcery to rival the versatility of Thaumaturgy, they could even be already Tzimisce allies in the Italic Peninsula. What's better is that their personal goals naturally keep them from wanting the same role of general leadership the Ventrue would covet.<br /> <br /> As a side note the Salubri would never be exterminated to the extent they was in canon. While the Tremere would be considered a bloodline by other clans, even if their power grew with their Ventrue alliance, the Salubri wouldn't be hit with nearly the same efficiency and would stay as a clan. But their zealotry also means they probably wouldn't join any sect. It is probable that the most common Salubri in modern nights would be Warriors, although the changes in social outlook could mean that the Healers would be starting to gain traction since the 19th century.<br /> <br /> Other clans wouldn't have a lot of reason to change sides in comparison, maybe even be more comfortable with this arrangement. Brujah and Gangrel would be at home with sect conflicts, hunting Ventrue and Tremere.<br /> <br /> My arrangement would be, in the end:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Camarilla</b></u><br /> Tzimisce<br /> Brujah<br /> Malkavian<br /> Giovanni<br /> Toreador<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b><u>Independents</u></b><br /> Followers of Set<br /> Assamites<br /> Ravnos<br /> Salubri<br /> <br /> <b><u>Sabbat</u></b><br /> Ventrue<br /> Lasombra<br /> Tremere (powerful Bloodline)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T12:40:55-07:00","id":1459172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459164#post1459164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you fail to understand that leadership and politics are complex,</div> </div> </div> </div>this is where you completly failed in your counter argument. what i'm talking about is not some obscure opinion regarding the complexities of politics and leadership but something so fundamental of being in charge of anything that you could aplpy it to anything. from organizing a session of D&amp;D to ruling a country as both a democracy and a dictatorship. in fact one of your later arguments is how the tzimisce apply the rules i've laid out.<br /> <br /> i do actually like how you pointed out the entire problem with this discussion, that being that in order to make the concept work you would have to either change the cam in both hierarcy, scope, goals, methodology and basically everything else or turn the tzimisce into diet ventrue with more horror powers or more laughably, both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T22:17:05-07:00","id":1459256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459164#post1459164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> <u><b>Camarilla</b></u><br /> Tzimisce<br /> Brujah<br /> Malkavian<br /> Giovanni<br /> Toreador<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Gangrel<br /> <br /> <b><u>Independents</u></b><br /> Followers of Set<br /> Assamites<br /> Ravnos<br /> Salubri<br /> <br /> <b><u>Sabbat</u></b><br /> Ventrue<br /> Lasombra<br /> Tremere (powerful Bloodline)</div> </div> </div> </div>You make some interesting points. I\u2019m not sure if this alternative timeline happens soon enough to stop Tremere from diablerizing Saulot or that general series of events from happening. I mean, it could, but I think I would personally want to keep the ascension of Tremere and the fall of the Salubri as similar to canon. I might switch them with the Cappadocians, making the Giovanni takeover fail or not happen and maintain the Cappadocians as a full Clan who enter the Camarilla, maybe with the Giovanni as a Bloodline. <br /> <br /> Do you think that the Ventrue would be so tied to the Tremere that they would follow them into the Sabbat? It seems like there would have to be some kind of internal turmoil within the Ventrue Clan to make that happen, like their own Anarch Revolt and overthrow of elders. Though the Tzimisce and Lasombra were both ruler Clans before the Anarch Revolts, maybe the Ventrue experienced that as well or instead. <br /> <br /> This is a slight tangent, but still closely tied to the thread\u2019s theme, what would be Sabbat be like under the rule of the Ventrue? Potentially it seems like it might be much different, especially lacking the Tzimisce influence. Would the Ventrue Sabbat be more moderate or would the Ventrue Clan in this scenario reinvent itself in the heat of the Anarch Revolt? I can imagine the Sabbat retaining many aspects of its character being controlled by the Brujah and Tremere: the violence and mysticism respectively, but it seems like it might be quite a bit different with the Ventrue in charge - which is alright, I\u2019m just curious.<br /> <br /> I like what you\u2019ve said about the different style of Tzimisce rulership. It would be more localized certainly, which would present some disadvantages. I imagine that in this scenario that Eastern Europe would be the heart of Camarilla power and that when events undermine stability in Slavic nations, Tzimisce power declines. Most notably Ottoman conquests and the rise of the Soviet Union. <br /> <br /> I still think it would be interesting to give the Tzimisce a rival Clan with new money that is eclipsing their worldly power. I don\u2019t know if that should be the Ventrue from within the Dabbat or another Camarilla Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T00:01:59-07:00","id":1459260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459256#post1459256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure if this alternative timeline happens soon enough to stop Tremere from diablerizing Saulot or that general series of events from happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>The diablerie of Saulot would probably have happened, because it was some centuries before anyway, along with the hunting of Salubri elders. But the campaign against the Salubri took several centuries and depended a lot on the Tremere getting traction. This traction came mostly from their service to the Ventrue, although there are hints to &quot;something else&quot; as writer recognition to the fact that it was too fast to make sense.<br /> <br /> But this is not something that need to be true, and even if it is, it may be interpreted in various ways. Particularly, when I say they would still be a clan I mean that the Kindred would refer to them as such, even if their numbers and collective power are lower than the Tremere's. Under Tzimisce influence the propaganda would loose some traction and the Salubri wouldn't lose clan status to &quot;that rabble of Caittif usurpers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally I like the Salubri <i>and</i> I think their presence would shake the status quo even more for this exercise, which is a bonus, but their actual numbers and power is entirely a matter of preference. Keeping the Cappadocians is also a nice change I'm totally in favor of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459256#post1459256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that the Ventrue would be so tied to the Tremere that they would follow them into the Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div>With other clans rallying under the Tzimisce, the Ventrue would need another power base. I don't think they would work as Independent, but I also don't think that they would have been welcomed in the Camarilla in this scenario in a position that suits them. So the Sabbat is the way to go. It could either be a plot from their elders or be for real, it wouldn't make much of a difference.<br /> <br /> And the Tremere was their big advantage in precisely that time period, during the war of the Ventrue from Hungary with the Tzimisce. The Ventrue had a history of using the services of mystics before, and the Tremere made it easier, cheaper and more consistent than it had been since Cretheus left the clan to follow Saulot.<br /> <br /> I must add, though, that I think this Sabbat would be very different, something I would have to work further to figure out. I always thought that, despite being quite fun, the Sabbat wasn't the most well though idea anyway. So instead of trying to think what the Ventrue would do in the Sabbat, think about what the Sabbat would be under the rule of the Ventrue and the Tremere, main ones, not <i>Antitribu</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459256#post1459256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a slight tangent, but still closely tied to the thread\u2019s theme, what would be Sabbat be like under the rule of the Ventrue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure yet, but I think this Sabbat would be far more linked to corruption than to violence <i>per se</i>. Instead of subtly influencing some institutions it could be far more hands on and offer its members benefits for cooperating with the sects complete control of a city. One picture I always had in mind when the core books said that the Sabbat is rumored to be this or that way, is that at least on the surface a Sabbat city would actually look the same.<br /> <br /> The difference probably would arise as a newcomer notices that the Traditions defended by the Camarilla aren't present. The Sabbat would still keep mostly the same hierarchy, credo and ritae, even because those things were mostly a Lasombra creation.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459256#post1459256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like what you\u2019ve said about the different style of Tzimisce rulership. It would be more localized certainly, which would present some disadvantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Advantages and disadvantages. I think it would have a less centralized style, because the Tzimisce wouldn't want the more central institutions to have more power over a domain than the local Prince. The Inner Circle would probably meet at the Carpathian Mountains, but would work more as a meeting of rulers than a ruling body, and Justicars and Archons would have far less leeway on their actions, but maybe additional diplomatic functions. It just occurred to me that the Tzimisce would resist the idea of the Conclave, but it could be implemented anyway through pressure of the other clans during the Convention.<br /> <br /> The major advantage of this system is that it would be even harder to harm the position of any clan or the overall structure even with something happening at the center. This Camarilla is less efficient at centralizing resources and efforts, but can survive quite ok even if the entire Inner Circle is wiped out along with the Justicars. Also individual domains are probably more prepared to deal with their problems, not just because they need it to compensate the lack of the Justicars, but also because they have a culture of local strength and the help of Revenant families. Those guys are a major boon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459256#post1459256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think it would be interesting to give the Tzimisce a rival Clan with new money that is eclipsing their worldly power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think both the Ventrue and the Giovanni (from within the Cappadocius, maybe) would do this well. They deal with the money, they don't follow precisely the same rules despite following something that resemble them, and they have their ways to screw with the &quot;proper&quot; rulers.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If something I said didn't make quite much sense, it may be because it's 4 AM here and I definitely should be in bed right now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T05:09:14-07:00","id":1459280,"title":"","content":"Oddly, I think the best way to have the Tzimise become rulers of the Camarilla would be to have the Tremere start their diablerie crusade a few hundred miles to the West. Imagine if they'd made the move to Austria earlier and went after the Ventrue rather than the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> 1. They still go after Saulot and company because the Tremere think his kind of the easiest pickings.<br /> <br /> 2. The Masquerade breaking Omen War doesn't happen. The Tzimisce don't march armies of ghouls and Vicissitude monsters across Transylvania.<br /> <br /> 3. The Ventrue and Tremere probably play a far subtler game of murder, influence, and death.<br /> <br /> 4. The First Inquisition still happens as Goratrix is SOMEONE'S sucker in France and gets the Templars destroyed but reveals to the Catholic Church that there are literal monsters among them. The Lasombra certainly didn't help, though.<br /> <br /> 5. The Tzimisce still have a huge civil war on their hands because Kupala and the Eldest are up to their own insane schemes. Dracula may or may not live long because the Tzimisce are far better in a position to resist him but I'm inclined to think his crusade against vampires (hidden by his impalement) still goes off well.<br /> <br /> |6. By the time the Camarilla is assembled by Rafaele de Corazan, the Ventrue are far weaker than they were before. I'm going to go <b>Alt-History</b> here and Jurgen never get kidnapped by the Elders of his Clan and made into the False Hardelstadt (assume that's true in this universe). He instead leads the honorable warrior Ventrue in revolt against his own Clan. Hardelstadt the Elder is still killed and the Tremere expose any attempts to replace him.<br /> <br /> 7. Vladimir Rustovich instead steps up to do a lot of the heavy lifting for getting his Clan to work with the Camarilla as there's still a revolt but the Inquisition is a far bigger issue for his kind than diablerie.<br /> <br /> 8. In this revised timeline, the Camarilla is formed of the:<br /> <br /> Brujah<br /> Gangrel<br /> Malkavians<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Toreador<br /> Tremere<br /> Tzimisce<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat are the Ventrue and Lasombra who have both eliminated large sections of their Elders. However, I'd imagine there's far larger groups of Lasombra and Tzimisce Antitribu in the Camarilla/Sabbat this time around. The former, I admit just because I think the conflict was ever so slightly suibtler and the latter because Vykos and Veyla are likely still Anarch Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> 9. The Tzimisce in this universe enforce the law of the Masquerade with horrifying punishments, impalements, and brute force more than the Ventrue. They take up a lion's share of the Camarilla being an autocracy rather than the softer power of the Ventrue. Still, it's not ineffective as, &quot;If you fuck up, you look like a Nosferatu for a year&quot; is a display that has its merits.<br /> <br /> 10. Anarch Revolts are more common in this universe due to the oppression of the new leadership and get put down with equal nastiness.<br /> <br /> 11. The Sabbat are even more occultist and mystical than they were before as the Tzimisce and Tremere dissidents are probably thick as thieves. I could see Dracula being one of their leaders in this universe rather than an Inconnu. He's a late comer to the party but that doesn't mean much among the Damned. Probably a bigger role for Lasombra occultists as well.<br /> <br /> 12. The Ventrue, though, have the reputation less as the merchant clan than as the &quot;martial&quot; Clan and they are actually able to keep the Sabbat generally always in straight lines than herding cats. I would make them much closer to being in full command of the New World then and maybe give them Washington DC and New York from the beginning.<br /> <br /> 13. By 2020, I'd say the Gehenna Crusade never happens (albeit the Beckoning does). The Brujah never leave the Camarilla but defect to the Sabbat, the Gangrel don't leave the Camarilla [The Tzimisce never deny the Antediluvians exist], the Followers of Set join the Sabbat, the Assamites join the Camarilla, and the Lasombra don't defect.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition is mildly more successful because the Tzimisce have never been as good at covering up shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-08-2021, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T19:05:22-07:00","id":1459386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459260#post1459260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...although there are hints to &quot;something else&quot; as writer recognition to the fact that it was too fast to make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I always write it off as the other clans finding the Salubri, to some degree, just plain annoying. Regardless how much the collective bunch of two-faced, backstabbing, bloodsuckers talk about how the Salubri were just &quot;the greatest and it's a real shame they were eradicated&quot;. Nobody, even other adherents of the Road of Heaven, wants some Helen Lovejoy type farting around everyone else's domains tut-tutting their fun.<br /> <br /> Though honestly, if we're going this route it does seems to me the critical fracture point would be the Omen War. Had the Tzimisce been <i>not quite</i> so buttmad over anyone but them fucking with their own, it may well have opened a door to at least a Tremere-Tzimisce detente (of which a certain Vykos would have been very unhappy, but fuck 'em) and kept the Tremere from turning to the Ventrue for aid. The Ventrue find their own dealings across Hungary and the Balkans much impeded, and Tzimisce likely manage to make headway into Serbia and eastern Hungary.<br /> <br /> The second fracture point being, thus relieved of external pressure and having more land for the knezi, when the Anarch Revolt breaks out it's far smaller in scale and the Voivodate manages to suppress it. The Eldest still eats it, but the clan manages to avoid ripping itself to shreds.<br /> <br /> I'd argue any sort of Tzimisce foundation of the Camarilla wouldn't be initiated by Rustovich, who by this point is still fucked off in the Carpathians mass murdering lupines and couldn't give a shit. Rather, the highest likelihood of it happening is at the hand of <i>Radu Bistri</i>, who isn't just respected among his own clan but <i>externally</i> as well, and knows how to pull the knezi's strings.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Ventrue are off doing...whatever. I'd expect, indeed, the Revolt would hit them hard and a couple vampires named Hardestadt would bite the big one anyways.<br /> <br /> The third big fracture point would be the Convention of Thorns. Since we have the Tzimisce in place of the Ventrue, when it comes to that little &quot;Assamite problem&quot; I'd fully expect them to just go ahead and say, &quot;fuck 'em&quot; rather than simply use knowledge of Alamut's location as a bargaining chip. Meanwhile, not even the stupidest Brujah would likely agree to whatever batshit terms the <i>Tzimisce</i> would have offered in place of the merely bullshit terms the Ventrue did in the actual timeline.<br /> <br /> So, as of the Convention, my thoughts:<br /> <br /> <b>Camarilla: </b>Assamite (albeit greatly diminished, with a <i>much</i> more severe curse, and likely all blood bonded or otherwise enslaved), Gangrel, Malkavian, Nosferatu, Toreador, Tremere, Tzimisce<br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat: </b>Brujah, Lasombra, Ventrue. But a considerably saner Sabbat. I'm thinking more &quot;DEUS VULT!&quot;-y than balls deep in ludicrous Noddism taken way too far.<br /> <br /> I don't see the Promise of 1528 happening with that makeup, so we can probably add Giovanni to the Sabbat as well. Albeit begrudging, distant, allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-08-2021, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T07:06:13-07:00","id":1459426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459386#post1459386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I always write it off as the other clans finding the Salubri, to some degree, just plain annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>As annoying as they were (and most of them were), actively hunting them shouldn't bring so much success in such a short time. It simply doesn't make sense, unless something else is happening. Keeping this something as still happening is a matter of personal taste, but hunting a clan already used to tough situations so thoroughly that in 4 centuries they just vanish, and doing that in the Middle Ages, simply isn't feasible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T07:32:24-07:00","id":1459428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459426#post1459426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As annoying as they were (and most of them were), actively hunting them shouldn't bring so much success in such a short time. It simply doesn't make sense, unless something else is happening. Keeping this something as still happening is a matter of personal taste, but hunting a clan already used to tough situations so thoroughly that in 4 centuries they just vanish, and doing that in the Middle Ages, simply isn't feasible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's worth noting their own founder was actively encouraging/manipulating their destruction (or at least wide scale reduction) as far as factors that helped that along. Stuff happened like clan elders that had managed to initially survive the hunts feeling Saulot himself calling them somewhere, and then, you know, expected results.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, something else was happening, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T08:05:43-07:00","id":1459434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459428#post1459428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting their own founder was actively encouraging/manipulating their destruction (or at least wide scale reduction) as far as factors that helped that along. Stuff happened like clan elders that had managed to initially survive the hunts feeling Saulot himself calling them somewhere, and then, you know, expected results.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, something else was happening, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is quite probable, but is a hindsight conclusion. I was talking about the specific line, and since we're working a <i>What if...</i> scenario, I'm trying to be explanation-agnostic. Saulot overtaking Tremere's body wasn't a thing back then, but that line made it explicit that the author recognized right then that this efficiency was strange, to say the least.<br /> <br /> And that efficiency is just a plot device. Ultimately it isn't the cause of the Salubri status in modern nights, it is the <i>explanation</i>. The cause is that the Salubri only appeared in the game when they were doing the first bloodlines, nothing else, so an explanation is needed for a situation that was already canon. The hidden cause is probably, in hindsight, Saulot's actions (given that at the time of original writing he being a master manipulator wasn't a thing, either), but it could be anything else or, in this scenario, not exist or just not be so effective.<br /> <br /> But yeah, on all probability and by hindsight in the canon material, Saulot was the one behind the Salubri's destruction. He may be responsible for Tremere's decision to diablerize him, even. Personally I don't think it would have been as efficient if the Tremere themselves didn't had such a prosper time after that, and the Ventrue had a lot to do with this prosperity. I don't think he cared about the &quot;clan&quot; status itself, either, and don't think the Tzimisce would go along with the same decision of naming the Tremere a clan just 'cause. Something that never happened in such fashion, bear in mind, even the Giovanni are far more a renaming of a clan than an offshoot being elevated and a clan being downgraded, since they are indeed Cappadocians, and the only ones around as far as most people know.<br /> <br /> Now, you can decide that Saulot was indeed that efficient, or that other hidden factors existed. I personally don't like the idea of a single NPC being so capable of effective control over so many minds, even an Ancient, at the very least I think other ancients would be interfering to prevent it. But in the end, that's a matter of personal taste, or rather, of editorial decision. I changed it in my version because I think it makes for an interesting situation and that's all.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just to be clear, I liked the propositions of both CTP and Theodrim. Particularly how detailed Theodrim's proposition went. My argument is about finer details and to foment a designer-perspective discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Praise were praise is due. 09-09-2021, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T11:38:14-07:00","id":1459455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459426#post1459426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As annoying as they were (and most of them were), actively hunting them shouldn't bring so much success in such a short time. It simply doesn't make sense, unless something else is happening. Keeping this something as still happening is a matter of personal taste, but hunting a clan already used to tough situations so thoroughly that in 4 centuries they just vanish, and doing that in the Middle Ages, simply isn't feasible.</div> </div> </div> </div>To elaborate on the &quot;annoying&quot; thing, I find it likely no small number of Salubri met their ends at the hands of clans <i>other</i> than the Tremere. They just lied about it and blamed the Tremere, as they were disliked, distrusted, and were hunting Salubri anyways, making for the perfect cover story. Of those who lacked the ambition, or were too shameful to do the deed themselves, throwing Salubri under the bus for boons owed by the much more utilitarian Tremere was also an option.<br /> <br /> It doesn't <i>necessarily</i> have to be down to some massive plot by Saulot or some methuselah(s), just down to the right people, in the right places, collectively ganking the <i>wrong</i> people, in the <i>wrong</i> places. Particularly if members of other clans were complicit, or even actively participant.<br /> <br /> Remember human populations were much smaller, and correspondingly Cainite populations were even smaller; even though mortal populations could support <i>more</i> vampires per capita due to comparative lack of technology and communication, the estimated population of Europe was still lower by an order of magnitude compared to today. Taking into consideration Salubri who fled or hid to be killed later, it would only take a few hundred Salubri deaths to declare them &quot;eradicated&quot; at most, as they were never the most populous clan by any source I've read. Not at least, compared to the likes of pre-Feast Cappadocians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T12:24:16-07:00","id":1459458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459455#post1459455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To elaborate on the &quot;annoying&quot; thing, I find it likely no small number of Salubri met their ends at the hands of clans <i>other</i> than the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is objectively true in the setting. Even the earliest mentions of the Salubri make it clear their reputation is as diablerists, soul eaters, and infernalists, and almost all of vampire society destroys them when found. They are widely hated. While the Tremere started the purge, once they convinced the other clans the Salubri were a threat, the others hunted them down. And since their numbers were not supposed to be large anyway, it wasn't difficult for their small numbers to be overwhelmed. (I think an issue for many players is that they imagine the clans are supposed to be near equivalent in size, and the idea of extreme disparity in numbers isn't a thing.)<br /> <br /> If we accept the story, it heavily implies the Salubri were likely already disliked and the Tremere evidence was merely a pretext. And depending on your personal tastes about Saulot, you might even add that Saulot intended his old lineages to be wiped out for whatever reason and perhaps even secretly aided those hunting them down.<br /> <br /> While I agree wiping out an entire clan should be difficult and require a long time, there's enough substance provided to justify the near destruction of the Salubri for me to buy in. I find it easier to believe than the Giovanni wiping out the Cappadocians, but even that was aided by later revelations that 1) Cappadocious had already eliminated a lot of the clan earlier in the Feast of Folly, and 2) the Giovanni actually weren't successful and there were lots of Cappadocian survivors in hiding.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T13:41:41-07:00","id":1459464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459455#post1459455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To elaborate on the &quot;annoying&quot; thing, I find it likely no small number of Salubri met their ends at the hands of clans <i>other</i> than the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered that, and no one was as numerous as pre-Feast Cappadocians. In fact, no one was as numerous as POST-Feast Cappadocians. The Salubri was far less numerous than any other clan since always, at least if you don't count Wu Zao and Nkulu Zao, that may or may not be particularly numerous. And they were already seen as a nuisance by many Kindred from other clans and had been hunted by all of them under the Purge.<br /> <br /> Still, they were far from defenseless, and the efficiency of the Purge is still strange without some other help, like Saulot helping it. Saulot makes a lot of sense, since he was effectively controlling the Tremere as their namesake, was a master of Auspex anyways and was deemed a saint by his followers. So he could easily locate his targets and communicate to convince them to reveal themselves.<br /> <br /> And I don't find either the Salubri or Cappadocius wiping convincing, although I don't find it so hard to believe they were greatly impacted, just not as thoroughly as it is normally implied. I don't buy that everything below 8th gen was killed. But outside that, my main concern was with how the Tzimisce would treat them if the Tremere and Ventrue aren't in the Camarilla. This is a naming convention more than anything, since in practice this is all that clan versus bloodline is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T15:39:47-07:00","id":1459478,"title":"","content":"I can buy one of the Clans being usurped and purged by another, as far fetched as it might be, but happening twice in a similar time frame seems a bit much for me. That is why I think I\u2019d personally say that the Cappadocians were never destroyed or purged, that the Giovanni are merely a bloodline of the Cappadocians, and that the Tremere did in fact usurp and mostly eliminate the Salubri - perhaps with the help of other Clans and potentially Saulot himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T01:52:02-07:00","id":1459526,"title":"","content":"My headcanon is that Malkav and Saulot are the same being. The question is whether his &quot;Golconda&quot; was before or after his insanity.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T03:07:26-07:00","id":1459530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459526#post1459526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My headcanon is that Malkav and Saulot are the same being. The question is whether his &quot;Golconda&quot; was before or after his insanity.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say after, because if this is the case we have a lot more recent &quot;Saulot&quot; activity than Malkav. And his development of Valeren/Obeah and start of Clan Salubri proper is far more recent. They are the younger of the 13, even if you consider the Wu Zao, that are older.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T08:21:26-07:00","id":1459558,"title":"","content":"The Tremere roughly rise at the time of guilds and universities. Appropriate<br /> <br /> The Giovanni coup works wonderfully because it represents a real-world shift of power where the mercantile class goes big and conservative guilds become an ugly dinosaur. Free market Capitalism Triumphs over the old ways and the Giovanni thus Triumph over the Capadocians. Very appropriate. <br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I feel the Capadocians/Salubri deserved to be shafted. A discipline spread of Fortitude+Auspex+Gimick isn't great for hunting and thus limits the spread of the clan greatly since they're essentially on hard mode for neonates. As diciplines tend to say a lot about personalities we can say they were obsessive and ready to take a beating over it... It's very condemning. I really have to wonder how these clans lasted so long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T09:39:01-07:00","id":1459564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459096#post1459096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we have the Camarilla:<br /> Tzimisce<br /> Ventrue<br /> Malkavian<br /> Lasombra<br /> Toreador<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Gangrel<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat:<br /> Brujah<br /> Tremere</div> </div> </div> </div>The first thing I\u2019d note is that this Sabbat would be essentially \u201cin name only\u201d as neither the Brujah not Tremere have a particularly vampire supremacist ideology (nor any degree of mysticism requiring a divorce from Humanity as Abyss Mysticism and Metamorphosis do), nor a particularly anti-Antediluvian focus; the original Brujah Ante was diablerized pre-history, Troile is lost beneath the salted earth of Alexandria and the Tremere have an \u201cactive\u201d Antediluvian as the head of their organization. In general, their focus would probably be less anti-Antediluvian and more a general anti-elder (except our own elders... they\u2019re okay) focus.<br /> <br /> Brujah and Tremere are also an interesting combination in that there\u2019s a clear divide between the physical (Brujah) and spiritual (Tremere) roles within the sect, not to mention each has their own preferred social discipline for influence.<br /> <br /> Also of note in this arrangement is that the Tremere would not have any incentive to cease abducting vampires to transform into new Gargoyle slaves as all their usual targets are now in the opposing sect; every one transformed reduces their enemy\u2019s strength and adds to their own.<br /> <br /> By contrast the Camarilla would become a more spiritual sect as with less adherence to the path of Humanity since the sect\u2019s head in this scenario hosts a number of alternate paths and the Lasombra and Gangrel\u2019s more traditional paths would thus be more likely to be accommodated and the traditional vampire-suprematism of the Sabbat would likely be a notable undercurrent within this alternate Camarilla. Without the push for secular Humanity, I wonder if the Roads would have ever been abandoned in the first place.<br /> <br /> I also suspect it would have interesting effects on the independent clans as well. To start with the Tremere wouldn\u2019t have cast the curse upon the Assamites since they\u2019re not associated with the Camarilla and I don\u2019t think the Kolduns would have the institutional organization to pull off a ritual of that magnitude. So the Assamites never have the Baali curse suppressed and have no particular animosity towards the Tremere. Given the origins of the Tremere as a Clan and how Troile became an Antediluvian, coupled with anti-Elder focus, the Brujah/Tremere Sabbat would probably have a working relationship with the Assamites in this version in a \u201cenemy of enemy\u201d (i.e. Camarilla elders ripe for diablerie) sort of way.<br /> <br /> For similar reasons (the Tremere can\u2019t really nitpick an Antediluvian diablerie... its also another case of a younger vampire supplanting their elder) the alternate Sabbat would probably offer more support to the Giovanni. With enough support there may not have even been a Treaty of 1528 and the Giovanni could even end up becoming part of this alternate Sabbat, reinforcing a sect philosophy of \u201cthe young eat the old.\u201d (at least as a party platform; Tremere and Augustus are younger than most other Clan\u2019s Methuselahs and even some of their elders... so while it might be wearing thin in the Modern Nights, back when this alternate Sabbat was being established it could be a compelling claim).<br /> <br /> The Ravnos and Settites would probably still be the black sheep they\u2019ve always been, but without the \u201cmust be on secular humanity\u201d aspect of the real Camarilla, this alternate Cam would probably have less of a reason to actively hunt them and the rebel nature of the alternate Sabbat would be a place they could survive if they chose to.<br /> <br /> Which finally brings us to the Anarchs. Without the militant anti-Humanity sentiment, this alternate Sabbat basically eats the traditional Anarch\u2019s lunch and provides a more organized resistance to the elders (with an even more rigid hierarchy thanks to the Tzimisce at the top) than just carping from the fringes of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Basically, this alternate setup is probably a bit more \u201cAlliance vs. Horde\u201d (with the Sabbat ironically being more Alliance with its alliance of warrior philosophers and Hermetics being at the top) than the Camarilla as the big dogs, with Anarchs yapping on the fringes and the inhuman Sabbat boogiemen \u2018out there\u2019 to keep the Anarchs from trying too hard to upend the established order.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also not a world where a Sabbat/Anarch take over means the city goes to shit because the Pyramid helps provide a degree of organization the regular Anarchs lack while also possessing a general adherence to Humanity-compatible roads that would prevent the need to drive up the misery index on the human population just because you can like the Sabbat might be tempted to inflict on those they basically consider \u201cHappy Meals on Legs.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T14:05:20-07:00","id":1459578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459558#post1459558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A discipline spread of Fortitude+Auspex+Gimick isn't great for hunting and thus limits the spread of the clan greatly since they're essentially on hard mode for neonates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the opposite impression. Fortitude + Auspex is a great way to survive and find prey. The greatest challenge in a hunt is to find and follow prey, and Kindred can overcome any hardship by pumping blood and the effects of the Kiss, I really don't see anything hard on this spread.<br /> <br /> And those two clans have &quot;gimmicks&quot; that are especially good for survival, probably among the most practical gimmicky Disciplines in the first levels. I find it particularly hard to see someone with either path of Valeren/Obeah as an easy target or someone with a hard time hunting, and Mortis, both original and Grave's Decay, isn't any worse.<br /> <br /> By the way, say what you may, the Cappadocians were canonically the most numerous clan by far. Numerous enough to go through the Feast of Folly and stay the most numerous afterwards, and that before introducing the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459564#post1459564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brujah and Tremere are also an interesting combination in that there\u2019s a clear divide between the physical (Brujah) and spiritual (Tremere) roles within the sect, not to mention each has their own preferred social discipline for influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only disagree with this divide.<br /> <br /> Although the Tremere are mystics, they are not spiritualists, they are hermetic mystics with a naturalistic bent. The Brujah, as political philosophers, would be the true spirit of the sect. Either way this Sabbat would be far less religious and more political, with the Brujah offering ideology and the Tremere offering bureaucracy and expert advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T14:45:56-07:00","id":1459584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459578#post1459578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only disagree with this divide.<br /> <br /> Although the Tremere are mystics, they are not spiritualists, they are hermetic mystics with a naturalistic bent. The Brujah, as political philosophers, would be the true spirit of the sect. Either way this Sabbat would be far less religious and more political, with the Brujah offering ideology and the Tremere offering bureaucracy and expert advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair assessment. Yeah, I was mainly thinking purely of discipline spreads (Celerity, Potence, Presence is a very &quot;charismatic warrior&quot; spread while Auspex, Dominate, Thaumaturgy is an archetypal &quot;wizard&quot; who divines, crushes wills and uses blood magic to win) where there's basically no overlap so each Clan can excel in their own areas without stepping on the toes of the others, but your point on philosophy is spot on.<br /> <br /> The Brujah win hearts both through Presence and using their superior physicality to win battles (everyone loves a winner), the Tremere identify and crush dissent.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it a little more, since the Lasombra are what infused the real Sabbat with its faux-Catholic trappings and they aren't a part of this version, I could see an almost more Arthurian mystique picked up by this Sabbat what with the Round Table being seen as more egalitarian, the associations of the Holy Grail with holy blood, etc. The Brujah are the Knights and the Tremere basically fall into the position of Merlin (advisor and miracle worker).<br /> <br /> Those two clans are an excellent foundation for an organization with much less infighting than having a Tzimisce-led organization that also included the elders of the Ventrue and Lasombra among their numbers. If they could poach even a fraction of the Nosferatu for their sect (very doable as they are rather &quot;Clan before Sect&quot; in their associations) they'd arguably be the better generalist Sect (all the common disciplines except the not exactly rare Fortitude and almost no overlap in areas of interest) than the alternate Camarilla (many of whom have specialist disciplines... Vicissitude, Obtenebration, Protean, Dementation... and a lot of overlap in areas of control at the top).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T19:32:35-07:00","id":1459611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459558#post1459558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I feel the Capadocians/Salubri deserved to be shafted. A discipline spread of Fortitude+Auspex+Gimick isn't great for hunting and thus limits the spread of the clan greatly since they're essentially on hard mode for neonates. As diciplines tend to say a lot about personalities we can say they were obsessive and ready to take a beating over it... It's very condemning. I really have to wonder how these clans lasted so long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I was never a fan of the Salubri. At least the core concepts of the Clan. There were some interesting things that happened later with the metaplot, but good compassionate vampires into Eastern mysticism who had a third eye and angelic names just seemed silly to me. They never played much of a role in any of my games. <br /> <br /> The Cappadocians, on the other hand, interested me a bit more and also seemed a bit too large and widespread to wipe out so completely in such a short period of time, especially for such a tiny upstart bloodline, and almost exactly like the Tremere.<br /> <br /> Of course, Auspex, Necromancy, and Fortitude aren\u2019t the best Discipline combination for finding prey. Then again, I don\u2019t see a Cappadocians neonate as just being thrown out and told to sink or swim catching what ever mortals that can. Established Cappadocians would surely have herds or influential ghouls who can give them access to blood, and the childer of such established Cappadocians will be set up with a steady supply of vitae. The Disciplines themselves are thematic in my opinion: Necromancy for the Clan Discipline, Auspex for mystics and scholars, and Fortitude the represent either relentless dedication to their pursuits or corpse like resistance to harm. In terms of utility, combining Auspex and Necromancy makes them information gatherers without peer. They can astral project, read minds or emotions, call up spirits to use as spies or provide information. In a modern Camarilla setting, the Cappadocians would make excellent advisers to more political and social Clans.<br /> <br /> V5 even kinda brought them back, though a lack of social Disciplines combined with a painful bite is particularly punishing for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T20:54:34-07:00","id":1459619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459611#post1459611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, Auspex, Necromancy, and Fortitude aren\u2019t the best Discipline combination for finding prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to run the Cappadocians as frequently feeding from corpses rather than the living, often using a minor Necromantic ritual to keep the blood potent for longer. This was even more common among the Lamia who, thanks to their flaw, could easily decimate a small village over the course of a year from feeding (not to mention many of them were Bahari and killing someone was a sin on the Path of Lilith). The Cappadocians also tended not to embrace on a whim so they would almost always take the time to properly train and prepare a new childe to ensure that they were capable of surviving on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T22:07:41-07:00","id":1459623,"title":"","content":"The issue of Cappadocian clan disciplines and the ways they feed came up half a year ago in the Clan Updates thread. For those interested, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438697#post1438697\">this post</a> makes for a good staring point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T03:25:00-07:00","id":1459639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459464#post1459464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, they were far from defenseless, and the efficiency of the Purge is still strange without some other help, like Saulot helping it...</div> </div> </div> </div>The other point to bear in mind, is this is the Medieval period through to the Renaissance, where transportation and communication were neither the greatest, and likely more importantly Medieval through Renaissance <i>Europe</i>. The quiet part of this that rarely gets spoken out loud is, &quot;...from Europe&quot;. As in, the Cappadocians and Salubri were eradicated...<i>from Europe</i>.<br /> <br /> Canonically, surviving Salubri were smuggled out of Europe by Assamites (and likely other Ashirra-affiliated vampires), despite their number having eventually dwindled to seven. And of course, there were the Salubri who lived in the far east relatively safe and free from harm. Last, and as already mentioned, the Salubri of the Laibon. And newer lore it may be, the Warriors simply decided that rather than wait to be killed off, they'd commit Suicide by Tremere instead and take as many of the bastards out with them as possible.<br /> <br /> With regards to the Cappadocians, the situation really speaks for itself. At this point in the metaplot, everybody and their cat found a way to dodge the purge, with only the genuinely stupid and <i>true</i> believers in Cappadocius' ridiculous post-Feast mandates sticking around to be eaten. There's Lazarus' brood and whatever fate befell them, namely whether they formed the Samedi or infiltrated the Ghiberti family (if I remember right); the ones who escaped to Kaymakli and eventually joined the Harbingers; the damn Harbingers themselves; ones who had the fuck-ugly version of the flaw and managed to pass as Nossies; the ones who by some miracle managed to claim they were Premascines and straight-up infiltrated the Giovanni...and, the obligatory Cappadocians in the far east and among the Laibon, who managed to escape Giovanni notice for likely centuries until the clan made inroads into those areas.<br /> <br /> That alone narrows the landmass in which these clans' &quot;eradication&quot; happened, immensely. We're down to one continent of seven. The requirements of &quot;eradication&quot; in an age with comparatively poor record-keeping, communication, and transportation is pretty much &quot;I've never seen one/haven't seen one in decades, nobody I know has seen one, so they really must have been wiped out after all&quot;. The memetic ball gets rolling, and suddenly <i>everyone knows</i> the Salubri and Cappadocians were exterminated.<br /> <br /> Realistically to me, that it happened -- <i>in Europe</i> -- is totally plausible. We're talking about a thousand dead vampires, tops, over the course of 400 years. Those are rookie numbers compared to what the body count of multiple Crusades, the Shadow Reconquista, the War of Princes, the Black Death, the Inquisition, and finally the Anarch revolt. And, vampires of the time were <i>clearly</i> not so stupid as to believe the clans were, to a member, wiped out, especially elders who are full aware how slippery vampires can be when pushed.<br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> where I believe the &quot;outside help&quot; came in: how this obviously false, logically-deficient, totally unbelievable narrative of these clans' eradication became memetically-driven &quot;truth&quot; in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T08:24:24-07:00","id":1459654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459639#post1459639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The quiet part of this that rarely gets spoken out loud is, &quot;...from Europe&quot;. As in, the Cappadocians and Salubri were eradicated...<i>from Europe</i>.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> where I believe the &quot;outside help&quot; came in: how this obviously false, logically-deficient, totally unbelievable narrative of these clans' eradication became memetically-driven &quot;truth&quot; in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interpretation I can get behind, thanks!<br /> <br /> But on another note, I really, really struggle with the idea that a clan needs more than Auspex and Fortitude to <i>feed</i>. This is completely nonsensical to me. What else exactly would be needed for a vampire to feed? Level 1 Auspex is the single most useful trait a predator can have, the ability to find prey and not lose track. You can get'em on their sleep if nothing else. Fortitude is excellent to find good ambush spots without worrying too much. Seriously, what does people expect a hunter to need!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T10:31:13-07:00","id":1459670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459654#post1459654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on another note, I really, really struggle with the idea that a clan needs more than Auspex and Fortitude to <i>feed</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you don't. It's utter, incomprehensible, nonsense.<br /> <br /> Feeding is only indirectly about one's discipline spread -- that is to say, if one is using disciplines as a crutch to build/maintain herds, or to &quot;brute force&quot; the act of feeding -- it's more about the company one keeps, and the social, economic, and political circles with which one involves themselves. Absolutely, certain disciplines make the act of feeding easier. In fact, I'd argue the single best discipline for feeding in the entire game -- for Dark Ages, anyhow -- is not a single social discipline in the game, but rather <i>Potence</i>. One good, hard, bonk on the noggin of someone who won't be missed, and you've got yourself a whopping <i>ten</i> free blood points.<br /> <br /> But, are they necessary? not by a longshot. If one's using disciplines as a crutch, one needs to either revise their character concept to decide whether it's actually viable, or their roleplaying style to accommodate a higher level of play.<br /> <br /> Hell, the flaw of healer Salubri is they can't feed on the unwilling. They trend heavily towards Roads where unwilling or deceptive feeding is, to say the least, problematic if not an outright sin. Even they have solutions -- cultivate herds that willingly donate blood. The ill, the infirm, the poor, or hell, just become a doctor or barber -- it's the fucking dark ages, bloodletting was among the most common therapies.<br /> <br /> Auspex 1 alone gets one 90% of the way to a &quot;successful&quot; diagnosis when considering pre-modern medicine. Diabetes was one of the first discovered and documented chronic illnesses in history; records of its symptoms and diagnosis date back to ancient Egypt. And until the 20th Century, one of the key tests to tell if a patient was diabetic, was to smell and taste their urine.<br /> <br /> Not that a clan of healers, or a clan of thanatologists, tend to favor medicine or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-11-2021, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T14:23:25-07:00","id":1459693,"title":"","content":"Regardless of Disciplines, I think it\u2019s too dangerous to really do hunting regularly. Finding random humans and drinking their blood, even if you can Dominate them, isn\u2019t wise and is not a good long term plan.<br /> <br /> Vampires need a herd, need ghouls, a slaughterhouse, a doctor or hospital - some steady supply. A Cappadocian, modern or ancient, would be no different.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind that a vampire\u2019s most powerful mind control is available to Cappadocians just like any Clan - the blood bond. It\u2019s a little harder to get someone to drink your blood without the ability to order them to drink and then forget that they did it, but once the bond is secure you having a willing slave who will procure blood for you or let you drink from them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Back to the Tremere and Brujah as the Sabbat. I do see this version of the Sabbat as less aggressively vampiric supremacist than the canon version, less mystical too. The Brujah would be the charismatic and idealistic leaders, the Tremere would be their viziers, maybe the manipulators behind the scenes. I could see the Brujah extending their Anarch idealism to the Sabbat - they aren\u2019t just fighting against elders and Antediluvians but also perhaps protecting all of society against vampiric predation. The goal of the Sabbat could be to create an ideal egalitarian society, we can throw some Marxist ideas in there too, since you know, Brujah. The Tremere wouldn\u2019t be so different, they would be hypocrites about the equality agenda, they are still ruled by their elders and the Pyramid still exists. This Sabbat could still oppose the Antediluvians, and the Tremere would just keep quiet about Tremere.<br /> <br /> The Tremere would be the monster makers of the Sabbat, making Gargoyles and other magical creatures to throw at the Camarilla instead of Blood Brothers and war ghouls.<br /> <br /> Since the Brujah are more dedicated to equality than the Lasombra or Tzimisce, I could imagine more mixing of blood with mass embraces. Maybe this Sabbat are mostly Caitiff. Clan loyalty could be seen similarly as many leftists see racism, as a tool that elders use to divide the young, so clanlessness could be considered preferred. Once again, Tremere would be hypocrites: all Clans are equal except the Tremere are more equal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 09-11-2021, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T06:43:11-07:00","id":1459748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459654#post1459654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interpretation I can get behind, thanks!<br /> <br /> But on another note, I really, really struggle with the idea that a clan needs more than Auspex and Fortitude to <i>feed</i>. This is completely nonsensical to me. What else exactly would be needed for a vampire to feed? Level 1 Auspex is the single most useful trait a predator can have, the ability to find prey and not lose track. You can get'em on their sleep if nothing else. Fortitude is excellent to find good ambush spots without worrying too much. Seriously, what does people expect a hunter to need!?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Advantage of Auspex is that you have an easier time looking for witnesses and can work out of people are really asleep or not. The hunting advantage of Fortitude is that you can run through a thornbush without getting caught.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you can feed without relevant disciplines... a few times. The issue is that without disciplines you need to be at the right time in the right place with the right people, you best have the right skills and attributes, and everything needs to go perfectly lest you suffer a reprisal (simply moving to another place isn't a great idea given how Domain is a thing) Murder isn't sustainable; without good disciplines you're not likely to be in a location that allows for weekly murders; that's prime Domain. A vampire who can only feed twice a week isn't a successful one. Disciplines provide a lot of leeway for vampires so that they aren't dependent on the stars aligning for food. Even if you don't use them, they add a confidence to the feeding process; knowing that you can effeciently fix things if you screw upreally keeps feeding from being a nerve wracking experience every single time. Auspex and Fortitude really offer a lot less confidence than the other disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-12-2021, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T09:38:42-07:00","id":1459755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459748#post1459748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, you can feed without relevant disciplines... a few times.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can feed without relevant disciplines consistently, unless you're a Giovanni or Nagaraja. You're completely overlooking the basic aspects of the Kindred condition.<br /> <br /> Every single Kindred have an intoxicating Kiss. You don't need to kill anyone, whatsoever, just bite. They'll hardly understand or remember clearly what happened unless you bare your fangs in front of them, which is completely unnecessary. You hunt at night, when a lot of dangerous things are already out there and few people will be able to witness anything you do, both for most being at home and for humans having a harder time seeing in the dark than you. Although not the most efficient tactic, you can use Vitae to increase your strength and overpower humans.<br /> <br /> Disciplines can help, but almost every Kindred hunting strategy, from seduction to invading homes at night, works fine without any of them whatsoever. You don't need specific supernatural powers, you need at least one dice pool of five dice in your sheet and figure out how to use it for your advantage. If you can't do that sure, you're not going to make it, but this is hardly a high bar even for accidental Embraces.<br /> <br /> Auspex and Fortitude help you with far more than that, but if you can't think of a way of consistently feeding just by being a vampire, that's another problem. What you need to be a good enough hunter to survive is to adjust to a feasible strategy in your hunting grounds and build up a Herd from there. One successful hunt every two nights is enough to get you through your unlife.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T12:29:21-07:00","id":1459760,"title":"","content":"Go to a prostitute and in a moment or intimacy, deliver a bite and drink a non-lethal amount of blood. She\u2019ll think she\u2019s weak from the amazing orgasm.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the modern rebirth of the Cappadocians, the Hecata, don\u2019t have this technique available to them, putting them at a huge disadvantage compared to Cappadocians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T14:06:25-07:00","id":1459764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459760#post1459760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go to a prostitute and in a moment or intimacy, deliver a bite and drink a non-lethal amount of blood. She\u2019ll think she\u2019s weak from the amazing orgasm.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the modern rebirth of the Cappadocians, the Hecata, don\u2019t have this technique available to them, putting them at a huge disadvantage compared to Cappadocians.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, they also don't look like walking corpses either.<br /> <br /> How badly decayed the Cappadocians range from &quot;Dress like Goths&quot; to &quot;Just short of classic Nosferatu.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4e/Phantasm_5_tall.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T16:15:11-07:00","id":1459784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459760#post1459760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, the modern rebirth of the Cappadocians, the Hecata, don\u2019t have this technique available to them, putting them at a huge disadvantage compared to Cappadocians.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kiss is so efficient on making mortals confuse with ecstasy that even Nosferatu can hunt just fine without Obfuscate if they can avoid to be seen just enough to bite. At a medieval night that isn't so insurmountably hard. The lack of the Kiss does harm the Giovanni and Nagaraja more than anything else. I don't remember now f the Hecata just cause more damage or also have that nasty pain that nullifies the Kiss on the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> But as far as hunting goes, those are the worse clans. Indeed, the Nagaraja are effectively crippled vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T18:42:29-07:00","id":1459802,"title":"","content":"Wait are you saying that a pale goth can\u2019t get someone in to bed?<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://images6.fanpop.com/image/photos/37300000/Evanescence-Amy-Lee-evanescence-37370729-300-316.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Seriously though, the default appearance for a Cappadocian is pale, like a fresh corpse, not anything like a Nosferatu. Even a Toreador can take a flaw to have an appearance of zero, but we shouldn\u2019t assume that is the default, as we shouldn\u2019t with the Cappadocians.<br /> <br /> As for Hecata and their bite, this is what the book says:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cSteeped in death, the fangs of the Hecata bring not bliss, but agony. Victims caught unawares will violently resist unless restrained, and few people submit willingly to the torture that is the Hecata Kiss.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> That is a bigger disadvantage than being cold, pale, and creepy - especially when they don\u2019t have social Disciplines. Not as bad for the Giovanni who have Dominate and are very wealthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T03:45:24-07:00","id":1459833,"title":"","content":"A hot goth? Haven't seen one of those in a while... and i think that was just on TV. Oh to be (relatively) young. <br /> <br /> It's not a hard rule, it's an insinuation, but Clan disciplines are really tied to the way those vampires hunt, and in a chicken VS egg argument, I'd say the way you hunt really determines what disciplines you get. [Nosferatu] was a legendary hunter, experienced in sneaking close to his animal prey before overwhelming them with power... so Obfuscate, Animalism and Potence became his natural disciplines. Your average toreador is famed for using their beauty in various noncommittal relationships alongside obsessive stalkeriffic behaviour for the few that do attract their attention... So the Toreador develop Presence, Celerity and Auspex. It's not that you can't feed without disciplines, but that you can't feed without eventually getting relevant disciplines... <br /> <br /> So the clans with a bias towards Auspex and Fortitude hunts... How? They're going to put themselves in harms way or through hardship and obsessively stalk their prey... That doesn't exactly scream prosperity. It makes me think Saulot and Capadocious were... very unsuccessful as vampires (if Incels had a discipline spread...). The former looking for consent, the latter presumably waiting for people to die... but people don't really die at a rate that's good for large numbers of Capadocians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T11:09:55-07:00","id":1459866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459833#post1459833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a hard rule, it's an insinuation, but Clan disciplines are really tied to the way those vampires hunt</div> </div> </div> </div>But you're treating it precisely as a hard rule.<br /> <br /> Disciplines aren't tied to hunt technique, Disciplines are tied to theme and personality. Hunting technique is related, but not in such a direct way. Even worse is trying to read an entire clan's capacity for survival just in the Discipline spread.<br /> <br /> As hunting techniques go, waiting quietly and detecting prey's approach is one of the most common techniques in the animal kingdom. Scorpions, spiders, crocodiles, are some examples of animals that rely on senses and patience. Carrion eaters like vultures analyse signs of weakness, disease and death from a safe distance and must be able not only to wait, but to withstand whatever's in their food after rot starts to take hold. Even eagles and lions spend more time searching and stalking prey than overpowering it.<br /> <br /> On vampires, a clan is more than just the way a vampire hunts, as much as it is also a part. You can read a clans overall <i>personality</i> in its Discipline spread, or at least compound it with other data to form a clearer picture. But reading hunting efficiency? Much less attribute its likelihood of survival based on the hunt? This is a lot of oversimplification and assumptions that go far beyond and ignore a lot of other things.<br /> <br /> So much so, that the lore stated directly that the Cappadocians grew out of hand, and in no moment they had problems feeding. It were their herds that started to feel pressure, leading to the Feast of Folly. Even after that, almost no clan was ever stated to face problems because of difficulty in feeding, much less because their spread was somehow inadequate.<br /> <br /> Cappadocius and Saulot were scholars and mystics, more focused on understanding their condition and the world around them. And with Auspex they could be just as selective with prey as they wanted to, as they could hear human activity from a mile away and inside their homes, see their auras to know their state of mind, look into their minds and so always find in an instants the perfect target by whatever standard they want, and never lose track of this target. This is the power of Auspex in the hunting scenario, to get exactly what you want and always know when and were to strike, in whatever fashion you prefer.<br /> <br /> This is reading theme and personality and tying hunting technique to it. Auspex and Fortitude talk about patience and selectivity. About understanding an environment instead of forcing change into it. About not letting fickle wants get in the way of your long time preferences. About not &quot;wasting&quot; time with feeding instead of your goals and about putting your ideals above instant gratification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T12:20:13-07:00","id":1459876,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> I feel strongly that Auspex + Fortitude+ inapplicable specialist discipline is going to be hard mode for neonates. They're definitely not useless, but literally everyone else has a better discipline spread than you when it comes to hunting. Great defence with no offence doesn't make for a well disseminated bloodline. Vampires need something like Potence, Dominate, Obfuscate, Animalism... even Presence and Celerity are better choices (They cost too much to use regularly but are really good in a hunting pinch.) <br /> <br /> under semi-competent mortal authorities, the only way I can see the Caps/Salubri thrive is if they became the pets of other vampires IE have a Ventrue, Toreador, Malkavian, Nosferatu or (god forbid) a Tremere or Giovanni look after them (Capadocious really did a smart thing bringing in the Giovanni) They use their advanced intellects and -specialist discipline- for the master and in return they are provided food, resources and a stable environ. Using ghouls to secure food for them is an option, but not a sustainable one. Warrior Salubri and The Capadocians have the disciplines and will to fight off other vampires for ideal territory but... not well. Remember that the Capadocians focused on the physical side of death magic for no good reason, rather than the ghost stuff that's actually useful. The Healers have absolutely nothing going for them without serving someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T12:29:43-07:00","id":1459877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459866#post1459866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On vampires, a clan is more than just the way a vampire hunts, as much as it is also a part. You can read a clans overall <i>personality</i> in its Discipline spread, or at least compound it with other data to form a clearer picture. But reading hunting efficiency? Much less attribute its likelihood of survival based on the hunt? This is a lot of oversimplification and assumptions that go far beyond and ignore a lot of other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I am a member of a clan of healers, or a clan of thanatologists. I have Medicine and I have Auspex, therefore I can examine and diagnose maladies in mortals, and treat them. Because bloodletting is one of the most common medical treatments of the age, I can feed in the most convenient, easiest, and simplest way possible that doesn't even approach the possibility of violating the Silence of the Blood. I literally do not even have to hunt in the first place, my food comes to <i>me</i>.<br /> <br /> Not that it's remotely necessary, I can give mortals tinctures and remedies that include a drop of my own blood, thereby bonding them. If a genuinely ill mortal comes to me, I can prepare a potion for them made of my own blood, and ghoul them for a short time so that they may heal -- bonding them to me regardless. And because I have Medicine, I'm not just slipping them snake oil to bond them, I'm actually proffering treatments that <i>work</i>. And for the unfortunate few too far-gone to help, I can at least offer them mercy in death without suffering.<br /> <br /> Oh look, I now have a herd. Likely, a far bigger herd than any other Cainite is capable in their own right. And, when word spreads that I can treat mortals' sicknesses, and they actually get better, I'll likely end up with Allies, Contacts, Fame, Influence, and Resources to boot.<br /> <br /> And because I have Medicine and I have Fortitude, I can actually feed from the ill without becoming a disease-carrier.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's apparently beyond some folks' grasp.<br /> <br /> Last bit, about feeding from the ill and not becoming a disease-carrier? Likely a <i>tad bit</i> important during the various outbreaks of cholera, typhoid, smallpox, and the like throughout the middle ages. And of course, the Black Death.<br /> <br /> And as a side note, as good a reason as any other why those clans were so easy to hunt and &quot;eradicate&quot;: they were easy to <i>find</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459876#post1459876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember that the Capadocians focused on the physical side of death magic for no good reason, rather than the ghost stuff that's actually useful. The Healers have absolutely nothing going for them without serving someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right up until some dickhead lays some beefy cable upstream from the village, digs a latrine too close to the well, forgets to wash their hands before baking the daily bread, or forgot to dump out the water butts before refilling them. Suddenly, half your herd's shitting themselves to death, the other half's in the church praying or already in the graveyard, and your stupid ass became a disease-carrier when you decided it's not <i>that</i> big a deal.<br /> <br /> Those healers and thanatologists won't be so useless then, will they? Hell, if you're very, <i>very</i>, lucky, they didn't cause it to happen in the first place, because you were a colossal dick to them and they decided to retaliate by attacking your herd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-13-2021, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T13:19:34-07:00","id":1459884,"title":"","content":"You want to trust a healer that only works at night? <br /> Even in the medieval, people didn't die at such rates that you could pull that off on the regular. And if you did pull that kind of stuff on someone's herd... well... they wouldn't give you the time to do it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T14:08:50-07:00","id":1459888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459876#post1459876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel strongly that Auspex + Fortitude+ inapplicable specialist discipline is going to be hard mode for neonates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already went on why I don't think it would for most neonates unless you cherry pick the lamest ones, but let me talk a little about the <i>inapplicable specialist disciplines</i>:<br /> <br /> Original Mortis, Level 2 is Blight, it costs WP instead of Blood, you roll with Dif based on the target's WP, which is below 5 for most mortals, and a single success is enough to cause -3 on all Physical Attributes. If you can't overpower a victim of Blight, then Potence won't do you any good.<br /> <br /> For modern rules, Path The Grave's Decay. Level 1 gets rid of a body in 4 minutes or less, Level 2 costs WP and freezes a target completely with an unresisted roll at dif 7, Level 3 will cripple any mortal if you really need to go this far.<br /> <br /> Valeren and Obeah have the same level 2 power, making a target sleep for hours with a touch. Against non-vampires it is one of the most effective attacks I've seen to simply end a fight and get the spoils.<br /> <br /> This isn't complete dedication to hunt, but hardly is it inapplicable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You want to trust a healer that only works at night? </div> </div> </div>The healer may live outside the village and have any number of conceivable reasons to not be around by day, and treatment isn't something that only happens at day. In hospices and similar facilities people stayed primarily at night anyway, so yeah, a lot of medical service happened at night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T14:30:52-07:00","id":1459892,"title":"","content":"The vampire could have a few ghoul or just blood bound apprentices around that could treat patients during the day. <br /> <br /> We shouldn\u2019t assume that the vampire just suddenly dropped out of the sky into a strange village with no contacts, friends, or mentor. Not many vampire childer can survive under those conditions.<br /> <br /> The doctor who only sees patients at night has apprentices who see people in the day. He has a huge number of villagers who love him and swear by the efficacy of his treatments. He\u2019s the man who saved your sister a few years back when her labor went wrong. You wouldn\u2019t malign the guy who saved your sister\u2019s life just because he spends all day in the woods gathering herbs?<br /> <br /> That is just one of a number of effective feeding strategies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T14:56:03-07:00","id":1459896,"title":"","content":"When vampires are first created, they don't have any Disciplines. Vampires are assumed to have learned their first Disciplines in the typically 5-25 years spent as a fledgling before their sire releases them. And not all sires give their childer extensive tutelage before letting them go out to hunt. Gangrel after all typically abandon their childer who have to figure out the methods of hunting on their own. So Disciplines aren't needed. They are just very, very useful. And yes, some of them are more useful - or at least obviously useful - than others.<br /> <br /> You learn to hunt by first going after easy things. Things that are weak and less likely to fight back or struggle much. Small animals often at first. Then when you move on to humans you pick the very weak ones first - the very old, the very young, the very sick. In Dracula, we see the new vampire Lucy first goes after young children who call her the Bloofer Lady (and of course earlier in the book, even the Count took a baby to feed his brides). These kind of prey typically don't require Disciplines. Then as the vampire matures, develops skills, becomes more confidant, and then adds Disciplines (both in-clan and out-of-clan), you tackle harder prey. Maybe at first it's drunks, drug addicts, and the like stumbling home. There's a lot of similarities between vampires feeding and sexual assault. One is basically a metaphor for the other. Or people otherwise abandoned by society living on the streets. There are various difficulty levels one does until one is ready to begin feeding on people relatively healthy in crowded places with lots of eyewitnesses and security measures. That's the goal a fledgling works towards. It's not where they start.<br /> <br /> By the time a Cappadocian is ready to be released, it's no more difficult for her to feed than any other vampire. Her hunting style, methods, and fallback plans already learned by that point.<br /> <br /> I think the Cappadocians more than most would need to feed on the weak, sick, and dying. But with Auspex they could find them easier, and they would know that not only could they overpower them (without Disciplines), but that even if the weak person was somehow armed or managed to wound them, that they'd easily survive because of Fortitude. In the modern era, I see even those without any special skills being able to survive among the street people - homeless, support groups, food kitchens and shelters, runaways living off the streets, etc. quite easily under normal circumstances. Those who have stronger backgrounds, special skills, more Disciplines, or more supportive sires have even more doors open to them.<br /> <br /> I don't need to agree with some of the specifics people have made here to think of any number of ways I'd approach hunting with a variety of Cappadocian or even Hecata concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 09-14-2021, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T10:42:06-07:00","id":1459941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459884#post1459884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want to trust a healer that only works at night?<br /> Even in the medieval, people didn't die at such rates that you could pull that off on the regular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than the constant outbreaks of cholera, typhoid, smallpox, flu, diphtheria, syphilis, the variety of causes of dysentery, malaria, and of course, <i>the plague</i>. And leprosy, which was so common an estimated 19,000 leper colonies existed across Europe around 1200 AD. That's all without broaching the topic of tuberculosis or anthrax, the former of which being a wasting disease the presence of which is well-documented throughout medieval Europe, and the latter so deadly it's the second-biggest theorized cause of the Black Death behind <i>Y. pestis</i>.<br /> <br /> And don't forget famines. Or wars.<br /> <br /> But other than all that, sure, even in the Medieval people didn't die that quickly. It's not like the estimated average life expectancy of the age, based on historical records and archeological evidence, was 33. And sure, childhood mortality brought that down, but it's not like ruling out childhood mortality only brought average life expectancy up to 55. In an environment where, depending on socioeconomics, families had an average of two to five children that <i>survived to adulthood</i> -- the number only dropping across Europe, following the Great Famine of 1315 and the Black Death, before bouncing right back in the early 15th Century.<br /> <br /> But, that's if and <i>only</i> if we were discussing Medieval <i>deaths.</i> Unfortunately, we're <i>not</i> talking about mortalities, we're talking about <i>illness</i>. And that was <i>plenty</i> common for an enterprising vampire to set up shop as a barber, anywhere they would like in medieval Europe, and have all the free blood they could ever want brought right to their doorstep, and getting <i>paid</i> to take it.<br /> <br /> Now, as for the rest...<br /> <br /> Can someone point me towards this parallel universe in which no one gets sick or hurt at night, the ill need no supervision or tending at night, and the ill simply teleport to a doctor -- or vice versa -- in an age where transportation was exclusively by foot or animal, meaning it could take hours to get someone medical aid?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you did pull that kind of stuff on someone's herd... well... they wouldn't give you the time to do it again. </div> </div> </div>Good luck finding out, in a world without modern epidemiology or forensic pathology. There's one and only one discipline in the entire game that would get you remotely close to cracking that case, if there was even cause to suspect in the first place, and it's the one these &quot;worthless&quot; clans have which you think doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-14-2021, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T11:34:18-07:00","id":1459950,"title":"","content":"To be fair things really weren't as bleak as most people think, despite all that. But diseases are common <i>today</i>, imagine at that time. And medieval doctors weren't paid only by their patients, many were maintained either by the community, the church or by local nobles to take car of anyone in need in the region. You know, sick or dead peasants don't work the fields and all that. And the greatest challenge for the time was sepsis, something that could take down anyone after a wound. By the way it was the greatest killer in wars across history, far more than the wounds themselves.<br /> <br /> But the game doesn't have only one Discipline that can crack the case in an outbreak. It have two. <b>Auspex</b> and <b>Healer Valeren/Obeah</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T11:47:02-07:00","id":1459953,"title":"","content":"Absence of evidence is not evidence of Absence! Execute him! <br /> <br /> I don't know if the Caps were ever as fucked up as the Giovanni, but Mortis is some despicable stuff. An argument doesn't need to be right, it just needs to be convincing, and I think it'd be very easy to convince others of a Capadocian's alleged wrongdoing. Some vampires are very charismatic, very rich, very good with prestation... <br /> <br /> You've also got the issue of the Capadocians not being the only doctors. Many Malks and most Tzmisce.. they're likely to be able to tell the difference between natural diseases and black magic. Any clan can embrace or ghoul a doctor, auspex isn't really needed it's just useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T13:07:14-07:00","id":1459959,"title":"","content":"If the Tzimisce founded the Camarilla, I wonder if they would have sided with the Cappadocians.<br /> <br /> The big issue being I suppose whether they had the balls to stand up to an Antediluvian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T13:36:18-07:00","id":1459962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459953#post1459953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if the Caps were ever as fucked up as the Giovanni, but Mortis is some despicable stuff. An argument doesn't need to be right, it just needs to be convincing, and I think it'd be very easy to convince others of a Capadocian's alleged wrongdoing. Some vampires are very charismatic, very rich, very good with prestation...<br /> <br /> You've also got the issue of the Capadocians not being the only doctors. Many Malks and most Tzmisce.. they're likely to be able to tell the difference between natural diseases and black magic. Any clan can embrace or ghoul a doctor, auspex isn't really needed it's just useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>And no one said any of that. The arguments were about those clans ability to survive, not any advantage they would have in a conflict with other vampires. Those, if they do exist (and they do), would be of another nature entirely.<br /> <br /> Mortis wasn't as fucked up as anything the Giovanni ever did. Indeed it was pretty tamed even compared with things like Dominate and Presence. And yes, since Malks and Tzimisce also have Auspex, they're quite likely to know the difference between diseases and black magic.<br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure of where you're trying to get to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459959#post1459959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The big issue being I suppose whether they had the balls to stand up to an Antediluvian.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> That wouldn't be an issue, that wasn't an issue to begin with.<br /> <br /> Generation doesn't make an Antediluvian, the same way it doesn't make an Elder or Methuselah. Giovanni and Tremere were both just Elders, not even particularly old ones, regardless of Diablerie. So much so that as a means to acquire respect Tremere's Diablerie of Saulot completely backfired, what really got them position in &quot;proper&quot; vampiric society was Meerlinda's work approaching princes with offers of service.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T18:04:25-07:00","id":1459982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459953#post1459953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if the Caps were ever as fucked up as the Giovanni, but Mortis is some despicable stuff. An argument doesn't need to be right, it just needs to be convincing, and I think it'd be very easy to convince others of a Capadocian's alleged wrongdoing. Some vampires are very charismatic, very rich, very good with prestation...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about that, most of the powers are pretty tame by the(admittidly horrible) standards of Vampire powers. the most awful is the debunked Candaverous animation where you put whats probably a spectre in a corpse. Everything else is about as nasty as the other Disciplines when compared to Demment, Dominate viscitude or even thaumaturgy<br /> <br /> <br /> Back on Subject I imagine the Tzmisce Carmarilla would be more decentralized a stronger emphasis on the princes soverenity in their domains, the toreador and Salubri would act as moderating influences with the fiends and the clan would have a shaper/rule/Koldun split where certain disciplines are emphasised. For example Dominate Tzmisce are more likely to be princes. The sect itself is more centered around eastern europe and has a stronger presence in rural areas. tzmisce are also more willing to personally fight in sieges which helps maintain the respect of the warrior clans.<br /> <br /> Carmarilla clans<br /> The patrician clans<br /> Tzmisce<br /> Toreador<br /> Plebian clans/bloodlines<br /> Malkavian<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Gangrel<br /> Salubri<br /> Ventrue Antritribu (clan culture is mainstreme vtm culture)<br /> Naraja<br /> <br /> anarchs:<br /> Brujah<br /> Ministry<br /> Caitiff<br /> large numbers of disenfrachised members of other clans.<br /> Samedi<br /> <br /> Sabbat Clans<br /> Ventrue (clan culture is antribu)<br /> Cappadocians (Lazerous kills augustus)<br /> Lamia<br /> Tremere<br /> Antitribu bloodlines<br /> <br /> Independant clans<br /> Ravnos (slowly shifting to Sabbat following week of nightmares)<br /> Assamites<br /> Lasombra-Lasombra arnt really independant but are present as kingmakers in all sects. rumours about the clan is secretly unified and co-ordinating via secret compact abound<br /> Giovanni bloodline<br /> <br /> In the Setting the Sabbat make heavy usage of Zombies and other blood magic contructs instead of mass embraces to counter the Carmarilla uses Ghouls heavily. Magic is more common knowlegue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-14-2021, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T19:21:57-07:00","id":1459984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459982#post1459982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carmarilla clans<br /> The patrician clans<br /> Tzmisce<br /> Toreador<br /> Plebian clans/bloodlines<br /> Malkavian<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Gangrel<br /> Salubri<br /> Ventrue Antritribu (clan culture is mainstreme vtm culture)<br /> Naraja<br /> <br /> anarchs:<br /> Brujah<br /> Ministry<br /> Caitiff<br /> large numbers of disenfrachised members of other clans.<br /> Samedi<br /> <br /> Sabbat Clans<br /> Ventrue (clan culture is antribu)<br /> Cappadocians (Lazerous kills augustus)<br /> Lamia<br /> Tremere<br /> Antitribu bloodlines<br /> <br /> Independant clans<br /> Ravnos (slowly shifting to Sabbat following week of nightmares)<br /> Assamites<br /> Lasombra-Lasombra arnt really independant but are present as kingmakers in all sects. rumours about the clan is secretly unified and co-ordinating via secret compact abound<br /> Giovanni bloodline</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite an interesting spread. I'm curious about the Nagaraja and the Ministry in those positions, and really liked your take on the Lasombra. It makes far more sense for them than their canon role in the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T23:57:17-07:00","id":1459999,"title":"","content":"Competition with other kindred is a fact of life and shouldn't be overlooked. The Capadocians don't have a competitive discipline spread, and in fact they benefit more from being small in numbers as they are a service-based clan without a particularly coveted service (Mortis is gross and there are better things to learn). IE the less capadocians there are, the less competition, the more in-demand they are, and the higher they can charge for a ritual. They're not the Tremere showing people attractive miracles, so they don't really need fortify or arm-up their numbers due to threats of others covetting their craft (being taken as a thrall is a possibility, but that's part of the reason why Lamia exist.) <br /> <br /> From a business standpoint, it just makes sense for the Caps to be small. <br /> From an ecological standpoint (how easy it is for Caps to feed) it just makes sense for them to be small.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T00:47:22-07:00","id":1460003,"title":"","content":"I think you're now stretching it too much.<br /> <br /> On the scale of clans competing many members won't even be restricted to in-clans to begin with. Or have them all, by the way. At such level it depends a lot more on organization and location than the 3 initial dots of a neonate.<br /> <br /> Cappadocians weren't Tremere. They weren't service providers to vampires. Some did, probably, the clan as whole didn't give a fuck. Tremere had to find something because they were actively trying to integrate with Kindred society, that was not a thing to no one else. They were politically ambitious, something the Cappadocians never had any interest in being.<br /> <br /> You're trying to base the idea that a Discipline spread doomed a clan on narrow assumptions that the game never made and don't make sense in context. No one is arguing that Cappadocians or Salubri would outsmart someone in the Courts of Love or anything. Just that hunting a clan to near extinction isn't feasible (convincing other that you did may be), because they already have all they need for basic survival and that isn't much. I'm talking Robinson Crusoe and you're talking James Bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T02:18:01-07:00","id":1460010,"title":"","content":"The only thing that really should stop the Giovanni from hunting the Capadocians to extinction is... well that's a lot of effort. But really, it's the weird state independents are in. How can the Johns really hunt the Capadocians as outsiders? <br /> <br /> Other than that, well organized clans can really wipe out disorganized clans if they want to. For the Giovanni, it's a good business practice. They're organized, much better at racking up prestation and resources. Like the Tremere, all they need to do is expand. The Giovanni can take losses much better than the Capadocians can; they have the systems in place to make replacement easy and their discipline spread is more frontloaded (immediately very practical) than the Capadocians. Frankly, without the Giovanni gaining a big enemy or the Capadocians finding a big and reliable thigh to hug, the Capadocians have no chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T03:11:25-07:00","id":1460013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459984#post1459984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's quite an interesting spread. I'm curious about the Nagaraja and the Ministry in those positions, and really liked your take on the Lasombra. It makes far more sense for them than their canon role in the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The nargraja are present due to the Tzmisces own predilections setting the bar lower for Carmarilla conduct, the geographical shift pushes the sect overall closer to eastern territories so exotic bloodline interactions become more likely. In addition I like to include the necromancer option for all sects. The ministry is more a nod to V5, I'd probably re-establish the gnostic aspects and see their support to the anarchs as resisting the Demiurge/Osiris' tyranny<br /> <br /> Lasombra Sabbat membership in Canon makes sense as a biproduct of the anarch revolt and realpolitik-it's similar to how China is a major trade partner of the modern economy despite on paper in simplistic terms it really shouldnt be. I've always thought people over emphasize the elegance of modern lasombra neglecting their dark savagery and disturbing occult revalations when the mask slips, in a way they remind me of batmans penguin (who happens to be a hot Goth chick) or a tiger that the airs,style and graces are quite real but never <b>ever </b>think of them as anything but an apex predator. I'm currently playing a Sabbat Lasombra so I've spent a lot of time considering how exactly Lasombra interact with the sect and clan history work. e.<br /> <br /> The suggested outline from my revision is the three sect emphasise differant aspects of the clans with les amis noir as a secret conspiracy at the dark heart of the clan. The clan cultivates a dispraportional amount of power for their relative presence simply because they're usually the primary alternative to the ruler clans of each sect<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460003#post1460003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're trying to base the idea that a Discipline spread doomed a clan on narrow assumptions that the game never made and don't make sense in context. No one is arguing that Cappadocians or Salubri would outsmart someone in the Courts of Love or anything. Just that hunting a clan to near extinction isn't feasible (convincing other that you did may be), because they already have all they need for basic survival and that isn't much. I'm talking Robinson Crusoe and you're talking James Bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortis isnt that bad a survival discipline their rituals and paths have a strong pragramatic utilitarian bent. They're just underdeveloped since the Cappadocians never refined a unified theory like the Tremere. A Cappadocians discipline lineup isnt flashy but it's a horrible mistake to think of it as bad. A cappadocian for example can survive off the dead far more efficiently than anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-15-2021, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T06:28:07-07:00","id":1460021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460010#post1460010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that really should stop the Giovanni from hunting the Capadocians to extinction is... well that's a lot of effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the point, although we seem to disagree on the fine differences in the task of winning over versus hunting to extinction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460013#post1460013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasombra Sabbat membership in Canon makes sense as a biproduct of the anarch revolt and realpolitik</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to analyse it as a designer, never thinking exclusively on terms of the canon explanation.<br /> <br /> The big problem here is that the sect behavior doesn't mash well with the clan outlook. And this is equally true for the Tzimisce. Many aspects of the Sabbat's ideology and culture make perfect sense, its history too. But the basics don't, the stupid ultraviolence that is OoC the <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i> of the sect. Making the Sabbat really be the whimsical bloodfest it was rumored to be and at the same time a political powerhouse was one of the stupidest ideas ever, the clans developed for it didn't made sense, and then a lot of effort was put in the following years to create reason out of this mess without outwardly assuming it was stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T07:29:48-07:00","id":1460032,"title":"","content":"You see the Giovanni could kill the caps, even though it's effort... because they just need to send wave after wave of neonates at the target. <br /> <br /> I think the Sabbat's pretty sensible so long as you moderate the o'l ultra-violence. &quot;special occasion&quot; violence, &quot;I may be a sadist but I'm aware that my actions have consequences for me and those I associate with&quot; kind of violence. &quot;Cuz I'm EVIL&quot; works for terrorism, less so when you're living your day to day life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T07:37:23-07:00","id":1460034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460021#post1460021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to analyse it as a designer, never thinking exclusively on terms of the canon explanation.<br /> <br /> The big problem here is that the sect behavior doesn't mash well with the clan outlook. And this is equally true for the Tzimisce. Many aspects of the Sabbat's ideology and culture make perfect sense, its history too. But the basics don't, the stupid ultraviolence that is OoC the <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i> of the sect. Making the Sabbat really be the whimsical bloodfest it was rumored to be and at the same time a political powerhouse was one of the stupidest ideas ever, the clans developed for it didn't made sense, and then a lot of effort was put in the following years to create reason out of this mess without outwardly assuming it was stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, I think of the Sabbat as existing for multiple purposes:<br /> <br /> 1. De-Anne Riceification<br /> <br /> The mechanics of V:TM mean that vampires are actually restricted from being as worse as human beings before becoming wights. This is kind of against the nature of vampirism as historically. The Sabbat provide an &quot;out&quot; so that you can have the bar scene from &quot;Near Dark&quot;, House of 1000 corpses, Salem's Lot, and other examples of vampires engaging in every depravity imaginable. This is even a playstyle that many players enjoy in small doses and why not.<br /> <br /> 2. To provide a foil for the &quot;personal horror&quot; aspect<br /> <br /> If the game is all about the tragedy of undeath and how it is a terrible it is to be a monster, you need people who utterly embrace the horrors of it. People who go well beyond Lodin and other &quot;evil&quot; vampires and are just vile. The Sabbat provide people who are intellectual monsters ala Hannibal Lecter at their best and monstrous animals at their worst. You could have done this with the Camarilla and Anarchs but the Sabbat is unapologetic.<br /> <br /> 3. To expand on the occult angle of vampire<br /> <br /> The Camarilla, until recently, was secular and Anarchs wouldn't know the Book of Nod unless you hit it with them. The Sabbat allowed a heavy focus on the mythology of Cainites and interesting angles to pursue with alternative moralities as well as demonology (which I feel is often overlooked--like people are ashamed of Sabbat who summon demons).<br /> <br /> 4. To provide antagonists<br /> <br /> The Sabbat certainly can be otherwise and I certainly have played many Sabbat characters over the years. But there's much to be said of the fact that the Sabbat really do make great easy monsters to throw at your players. BLOODLINES is all about the conflict between La Croix and the Anarchs before, suddenly, there's a bunch of baby eating psychopaths trying to kill you.<br /> <br /> It actually adds an interesting &quot;Enemy Mine&quot; situation with the Anarchs and Camarilla as both will side with each other against the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> 5. To fill in vampire history<br /> <br /> Why does the Camarilla exist? Why are the Anarchs so chummy with the Camarilla they ostensibly hate? Much of the past 1000 years is defined by the Sabbat's subtle and unsubtle influence.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, the Lasombra and Tzimicse both fit into the Sabbat but they also should fit into the Camarilla and Anarchs too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-16-2021, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T07:38:58-07:00","id":1460036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460032#post1460032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see the Giovanni could kill the caps, even though it's effort... because they just need to send wave after wave of neonates at the target.<br /> <br /> I think the Sabbat's pretty sensible so long as you moderate the o'l ultra-violence. &quot;special occasion&quot; violence, &quot;I may be a sadist but I'm aware that my actions have consequences for me and those I associate with&quot; kind of violence. &quot;Cuz I'm EVIL&quot; works for terrorism, less so when you're living your day to day life.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I don't think that strategy is all that effective actually. Also, the Giovanni are the one group that actually cannot do that because they only Embrace their relatives. As we see with shovelheads, I think it's also a terrible strategy versus planned assassinations.<br /> <br /> 2. It depends if you think that's missing the point or not. The Sabbat are guys whose hat is, &quot;Revel in the Beast's worst impulses.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T08:01:27-07:00","id":1460039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460021#post1460021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big problem here is that the sect behavior doesn't mash well with the clan outlook. And this is equally true for the Tzimisce. Many aspects of the Sabbat's ideology and culture make perfect sense, its history too. But the basics don't, the stupid ultraviolence that is OoC the <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i> of the sect. Making the Sabbat really be the whimsical bloodfest it was rumored to be and at the same time a political powerhouse was one of the stupidest ideas ever, the clans developed for it didn't made sense, and then a lot of effort was put in the following years to create reason out of this mess without outwardly assuming it was stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll agree with that assessment. I know in my own games I\u2019ve always had to lean hard on the religious fanaticism of the \u201cSword of Caine\u201d angle where the ultra-violence is a political tool akin to various State sponsors of terrorism who supply resources to violent extremists to destabilize their enemies without getting directly involved in a war themselves.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat makes a lot of sense if you use a similar two-tiered approach. The Lasombra and Tzimisce (particularly their elders) are the \u201cState Sponsors\u201d while the rank and file Antitribu packs are the \u201cTerrorists\u201d funded to keep their enemies off balance.<br /> <br /> What holds it all together is the religious fundamentalism underlying it and the belief by the cannon fodder that the \u201cState\u201d shares their beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T08:35:56-07:00","id":1460044,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean the Giovann would shovelhead. It's more like this.<br /> <br /> *Venice*<br /> Alphonso, now that you've been embraced, go to Barcelona, take a few family members, establish yourself, keep in contact.<br /> 12 years later<br /> Alphonso, We're going to execute order 66 soon, I'm going to send you your second-nephew Cecilia, you give her what she needs.<br /> 2 years later<br /> Alphonso, I'm sad to hear Cecilia failed, I've sent Benito, take good care of him. Perhaps embrace while you're there.<br /> 5 years later<br /> Benito, A shame about alphonso, you'll take over for him. I hope Dianna finds you well. She's very experienced. Put your trust in her.<br /> <br /> At some point, the Capadocian is going to die.<br /> The Tremere are even better at this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T09:52:19-07:00","id":1460052,"title":"","content":"I don't foresee the Giovanni winning by embracing more than the Cappadocians, especially since the Cappadocians had larger numbers to start with of older more established vampires. When it comes to childer as well, they often wont even have the Clan Disciplines that are supposed to be what makes the Giovanni superior. Sure, the Giovanni can embrace cannon fodder, but the Cappadocians could potentially do that too and their new childer don't have to rely as much on Disciplines since they have the Kiss.<br /> <br /> As for the Cappadocians surviving if the Tzimisce rule the Camarilla? Sure, that is possible, it depends on what exactly we wanted to do with the scenario, but there could be a number of plausible events that could make that happen. For whatever reason, Cappadocius doesn't allow himself to be diablerized, and that is that. If he is diablerized and the Giovanni start trying to destroy the Cappadocians, the Tzimisce might say &quot;Hey, we can't let another version of the Tremere spring up.&quot; and throw the weight of the Camarilla behind protecting the Cappadocians: in which case we would have Cappadocians in the Camarilla and perhaps Giovanni in the Sabbat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T11:57:19-07:00","id":1460074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460052#post1460052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't foresee the Giovanni winning by embracing more than the Cappadocians, especially since the Cappadocians had larger numbers to start with of older more established vampires. When it comes to childer as well, they often wont even have the Clan Disciplines that are supposed to be what makes the Giovanni superior. Sure, the Giovanni can embrace cannon fodder, but the Cappadocians could potentially do that too and their new childer don't have to rely as much on Disciplines since they have the Kiss.<br /> <br /> As for the Cappadocians surviving if the Tzimisce rule the Camarilla? Sure, that is possible, it depends on what exactly we wanted to do with the scenario, but there could be a number of plausible events that could make that happen. For whatever reason, Cappadocius doesn't allow himself to be diablerized, and that is that. If he is diablerized and the Giovanni start trying to destroy the Cappadocians, the Tzimisce might say &quot;Hey, we can't let another version of the Tremere spring up.&quot; and throw the weight of the Camarilla behind protecting the Cappadocians: in which case we would have Cappadocians in the Camarilla and perhaps Giovanni in the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what I'm referring to is the fact that after Cappadocias was diablized by Augustus Giovanni but only a small amount of his power was taken due to Cappadocias not letting his soul being devoured, Japath and the other Cappadocians petitioned the Camarilla for membership/protection.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla made the Promise instead with the Giovanni and left the Cappadocians to twist in the wind.<br /> <br /> Which is the FIRST example of the &quot;Camarilla is everyone's friend&quot; being shown to be complete bullshit.<br /> <br /> Now the Tzimisce might do the same or they might actually take the war to Augustus Giovanni. Especially since, as it seems in 5th Edition, Augustus the Antediluvian is a paper tiger.<br /> <br /> Tremere as an Antediluvian was capable of melting people and resurrecting the dead and to look at him with Auspex could drive a Kindred insane. Augustus? Not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T12:19:53-07:00","id":1460078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460021#post1460021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of the point, although we seem to disagree on the fine differences in the task of winning over versus hunting to extinction.<br /> <br /> <br /> I tend to analyse it as a designer, never thinking exclusively on terms of the canon explanation.<br /> <br /> The big problem here is that the sect behavior doesn't mash well with the clan outlook. And this is equally true for the Tzimisce. Many aspects of the Sabbat's ideology and culture make perfect sense, its history too. But the basics don't, the stupid ultraviolence that is OoC the <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i> of the sect. Making the Sabbat really be the whimsical bloodfest it was rumored to be and at the same time a political powerhouse was one of the stupidest ideas ever, the clans developed for it didn't made sense, and then a lot of effort was put in the following years to create reason out of this mess without outwardly assuming it was stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think 3rd ed had the best spin on it with the terrorist army of the night. A lot of the dumber stuff was downplayed and refined into a cold nasty callous disregard for humans and humanity and a siege mentality Which works quite well for both clans and their interactions with the anti's I always used the comparison of a skin head vs a gestapo officer in relation to shovel head trash vs an actual lasombra Superficially they look very differant but if you mistake the snazzy uniform and competency for anything resembling class or reason you're in for a very very bad day","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-15-2021, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T14:25:59-07:00","id":1460085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460032#post1460032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see the Giovanni could kill the caps, even though it's effort... because they just need to send wave after wave of neonates at the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not how hunting works. It is not a siege, it is a search.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460034#post1460034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, I think of the Sabbat as existing for multiple purposes:</div> </div> </div> </div>And I agree with every single one of them, yet here comes the problem:<br /> <br /> It isn't about the Sabbat itself, but about the places the Sabbat controls.<br /> <br /> By portraying the Sabbat the way it does, VtM delves in the practice of portraying their chosen cities as cesspools of unimaginable violence where nothing makes sense. Because no, they're not portrayed as sensible monsters that at least know how to keep the masquerade, they're portrayed as unstoppable lunatics engaging in their antics with full supernatural might every night, raging across the streets in plain sight.<br /> <br /> What does that tell you about the places they live in? And which places were chosen for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T16:22:02-07:00","id":1460095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460085#post1460085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... not how hunting works. It is not a siege, it is a search.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I agree with every single one of them, yet here comes the problem:<br /> <br /> It isn't about the Sabbat itself, but about the places the Sabbat controls.<br /> <br /> By portraying the Sabbat the way it does, VtM delves in the practice of portraying their chosen cities as cesspools of unimaginable violence where nothing makes sense. Because no, they're not portrayed as sensible monsters that at least know how to keep the masquerade, they're portrayed as unstoppable lunatics engaging in their antics with full supernatural might every night, raging across the streets in plain sight.<br /> <br /> What does that tell you about the places they live in? And which places were chosen for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the mutant hating Mordor of the North, obviously. Canada, Home of Wolverine and William Shatner.<br /> <br /> Which I am only half-kidding about if anyone else remembers the disclaimer to Montreal by Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-15-2021, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-16T16:40:04-07:00","id":1460154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1459953#post1459953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and I think it'd be very easy to convince others of a Capadocian's alleged wrongdoing. Some vampires are very charismatic, very rich, very good with prestation...</div> </div> </div> </div>...and who do those very charismatic, rich and prestation-laden, Cainites turn to when their food starts taking sick and dying <i>en masse</i> due to disease outbreak, and those same Cainites are liable to become disease-carriers and plague-bearers for it? Might it be, perchance, those among them who have studied life, death, and everything in between, who have intimate knowledge of human physiology due to their practices, as well as varieties of medicine many of which fell out of human knowledge centuries prior?<br /> <br /> And who, having a near-monopoly on that knowledge, can then charge a premium? For someone who wants to talk a big economics game, you've forgotten four things:<br /> <br /> 1. what we're talking about is a <i>seller's</i> market,<br /> 2. it's a seller's market of a service with highly elastic supply, but inelastic demand,<br /> 3. it's a seller's market dominated by a <i>de facto</i> cartel with an indefinitely-long memory, and,<br /> 4. it's a seller's market of a service the provision of which is quite literally a matter of life and death.<br /> <br /> In other words, you really, <i>really</i>, don't want to piss off your vendors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You've also got the issue of the Capadocians not being the only doctors. Many Malks and most Tzmisce.. they're likely to be able to tell the difference between natural diseases and black magic. Any clan can embrace or ghoul a doctor, auspex isn't really needed it's just useful. </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, the notoriously rational, stable, and reliable Malkavians. And, the renowned custodians of humanity and insightful cultivators of the kine, who are always ready and willing to lend a healing hand, the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> How could I have possibly forgotten.<br /> <br /> And of course, the blackest of all black magics, unhallowed ground upon which even Nephandi dare to tread: digging a shithole too close to the well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-16-2021, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-16T23:45:22-07:00","id":1460185,"title":"","content":"most vampires can weather a plague. They're immune. Vampires really only need to avoid blood born diseases to boot. If it isn't in the blood, they're unlikely to spread it. Besides that, I think you're really overselling Capadocian expertise. The only thing that separates them from the mortal Barber-surgeons are heightened senses and actual magic, and actual magic leads them into many traps and pitfalls. There isn't a spell of &quot;cure disease&quot;. At best the thaumaturges (not the Necrophiles) have a ritual to cleanse a cup of blood.<br /> <br /> ...and the Malkavians really aren't that unpredictable, at least when they're out of the hands of players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T16:50:12-07:00","id":1460268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460185#post1460185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're immune.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their food <i>isn't</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires really only need to avoid blood born diseases to boot. </div> </div> </div>Which is most diseases, really, once you take into consideration pathogens spread by other vectors, but can and will also be found in blood samples because relevant pathogens infiltrate the circulatory system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it isn't in the blood, they're unlikely to spread it. </div> </div> </div>The hell they aren't. Taking the question of blood entirely out of the equation, we're discussing immortal creatures that exist in a perpetual state of stasis. They can and do still be contaminated by parasites (who, especially for <i>certain</i> clans and bloodlines, the parasites will feed from the vampire and become<i> ghoul</i> parasites), and their fingernails and mouths are still vectors for contamination especially in the Dark Ages when, even under the best of circumstances, hygiene and sanitation are woefully lacking compared to the modern era.<br /> <br /> Which is why the disease-carrier flaw isn't limited exclusively blood-borne diseases, in contrast to your earlier claim. One of the diseases explicitly mentioned in the flaw's very write-up is rabies, decidedly <i>not</i> a blood-borne disease.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only thing that separates them from the mortal Barber-surgeons are heightened senses and actual magic, and actual magic leads them into many traps and pitfalls. </div> </div> </div>...and being immortal creatures for whom the sum total of human knowledge of medicine, from the earliest discovered papyruses and Greek treatises all the way to a given chronicle's date, is at their fingertips. Spread via oral tradition, sure, but when your educator may have been the very author of those papyruses and treatises who since had centuries to hone their craft, oral tradition suddenly counts for a <i>whole</i> lot more in an age the mortals are still enamored with the likes of humorism and miasma theory.<br /> <br /> For once, rather than stubbornly cleave to your own misguided preconceptions about what VtDA and VtM <i>ought</i> to be and refuse any counter-argument otherwise because it conflicts with your -- clearly, at this point -- partisan worldview, take a moment to consider the full implications of what vampirism actually would be and how vampires of radically different skillsets would actually behave within their own social ecosystem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T23:33:36-07:00","id":1460305,"title":"","content":"And the Greeks were often <i>wrong</i>. Sure a capadocian might have centuries of experience, the ability to increase their attributes over the years, and most importantly they're going to be some of the few who dare to conduct autopsies, but how much do you think they are going to teach to their childer? there are far more pressing things to teach a fledgling than medicine, and a sire isn't likely to be willing to spend all their time teaching a childe, childer are embraced to do things, and nothing impoverishes a master like teaching everything he knows. An elder might be an unfathomable fountain of knowledge concerning archaic and often bogus medicine, but his childer and most of the clan really aren't going to be much better than a ghouled barber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T03:58:12-07:00","id":1460315,"title":"","content":"I have maybe five minutes before I have to work, but I think I can bang this out in that time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460305#post1460305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Greeks were often <i>wrong</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The relevance of that statement is...what, now? You only contradict it by highlighting the importance of longer-term, holistic, education that only vampires would have access to, in this same post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An elder might be an unfathomable fountain of knowledge concerning archaic and often bogus medicine... </div> </div> </div>Mortals in the Dark Ages get maybe thirty years' life expectancy as an adult to learn and practice their trade. That's a point many vampires, but especially scholastically-inclined ones, aren't even released yet. Are we beginning to see the contradiction?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but how much do you think they are going to teach to their childer? there are far more pressing things to teach a fledgling than medicine, and a sire isn't likely to be willing to spend all their time teaching a childe,..childer are embraced to do things, and nothing impoverishes a master like teaching everything he knows. </div> </div> </div>Let me get this straight.<br /> <br /> After an entire thread arguing Mortis is the only hat upon which Cappadocians can hang their hat to make them distinct and unique, your argument is...sires just aren't going to bother teaching childer the one knowledge used in basically every Mortis level, path, and ritual. And that, in contradiction to their clan write-up, they're not going to eye those with pre-existing talent or experience in it.<br /> <br /> What's next, Tzimisce that don't arse themselves teaching Body Crafts, or Tremere that don't bother teaching Occult? Ventrue that just decide Leadership isn't something to bother with in educating childer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-18-2021, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T04:24:10-07:00","id":1460317,"title":"","content":"Does a child now need 5 dots to use Mortis? Does a sire have time to teach them that? <br /> <br /> Fortitude is not a great hunting discipline<br /> Auspex is not a great hunting discipline. <br /> Morits apparently requires massive amounts of pre-modern medical knowledge. So either the sire needs to invest a lot of time into a knowledge (in addition to teaching them the rules and regulations of undead society, how to feed without getting caught and so on) or the sire can embrace some of the very few medical experts to save themselves a lot of time. Neither option looks great if you want Capadocians to be a big, thriving bloodline on par with any of the big six. And you still haven't adressed how the more Capadocians there are, the less valuable their services. <br /> <br /> Fact is, Neonate Capadocians are disadvantaged. I'm not saying they can't work, but literally every other clan is going to have easier early nights than them. Even clans that struggle, like the Tzmisce and Ravnos, have an easier time than Cappadocians. It's only natural that they were replaced by the Giovanni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T07:29:46-07:00","id":1460327,"title":"","content":"Cappadocians dedicating their existence to academic search is literally their basic clan write-up. And academy works with education of new students since always. It is not just that students form the next generation of researchers, a lot of living, breathing teachers wouldn't give a fuck for the next generations. Teaching is less time-consuming than learning in the first place, can be done during actual research work, and make for better helpers and colleagues.<br /> <br /> Not only that, in academy you pretty much acquire prestige, status and patronage by showing-off your genius through spreading your knowledge instead of hoarding it. This is how medicine, astronomy, philosophy and everything else works since down of time. You may make your knowledge obscure for outsiders, but you pretty much need to spread among your peers and students to be effective at your trade. Otherwise you only get to be ineffectual, isolated and poor.<br /> <br /> That's before we even get to the point were a neonate with Auspex tend to learn far quicker than a Ghoul and will eventually have decades of experience themselves, that being devoted to those studies the clan naturally share knowledge and theories, so there is a collective building of understanding, or that by dealing with the very state of the body after <i>and before</i> death Mortis not only requires knowledge in Medicine, but also gives intimate experience with the workings of the human body. Or even the simplest fact that you can teach a fledgling by giving them books, tests and whatnot that can be reused and passed down to teach many others with minimal effort for the teacher.<br /> <br /> Above all, it is simply what is written in the books. Clanbook Cappadocian, for example, reinforces regularly that the clan dedicates itself to the study of medicine, that they are a scholar society first and foremost, that despite the teaching not going far inside the sire-childe relation specifically, they share knowledge a lot in their yearly meetings. That every member is expected to study and collaborate to the clan collective knowledge. To say that Cappadocians aren't more knowledgeable in Medicine is simply to ignore the official lore altogether for the benefit of one's own vision of how it should be.<br /> <br /> I'm not addressing the other arguments anymore, they were extensively discussed already and I already know they'll simply be ignored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T07:41:14-07:00","id":1460329,"title":"","content":"Bah, the Feast of Folly was the smartest move of any Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> Get rid of the dead weight!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-18-2021, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T10:26:42-07:00","id":1460348,"title":"","content":"Do you think all this academic focus will aid in making them a big and powerful clan? It just seems like the other clans have more practical things to do with their time. Yes the capadocians might work out how to deliberately sicken someone, or how to save part of a herd, but is that really stronger than wealth, power and influence? The Blood supply issue also eats into research time. Plus An issue with guilds was that they stiffled innovation: If a respected elder says X is Y , and he's wrong, going against him may be a political issue, and you may have to keep your research to yourself as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T10:48:44-07:00","id":1460350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460348#post1460348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think all this academic focus will aid in making them a big and powerful clan?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but that only seems to be an issue to you.<br /> <br /> You don't need to be powerful to survive, you don't need to be powerful to eke out a living, you don't need to be powerful to do research...<br /> <br /> The thread is about the Tzimisce ruling the Camarilla, not the Cappadocians or Salubri rulling the Camarilla. The Cap/Sal side discussion is just about how believable it is for those clans to be exterminated or not, and even that just 'cause some people here thinks they're good additions to the alternative make-up of the sects. You know, the make-up that will have &quot;non-powerful&quot; clans anyway.<br /> <br /> Even among the many that still would let one or both those clans out, you're the only one saying that they would die because of their Discipline spread instead of any other reason and then creating assumptions to back it up since there is no backup for your claims in the actual books. &quot;Forcing&quot; us to counter your assumptions in an unending rabbit hole of non-backed claims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T15:11:02-07:00","id":1460372,"title":"","content":"I mean its not as though you even really need disciplines to hunt, the bites pretty awesome on it's own and frankly it isnt hard to feed on people in my experience as long as your social stats are okay, you're good at sneaking or you're smart and figured something out.<br /> <br /> it's also a pretty weird line of reasoning the Cappadocians specifically were doomed because their disciplines wernt mini maxed enough to hunting people. Frankly I got the impression they drank from the dead a lot of the time anyway, they even had a level one ritual to ring extra vitae out of corpses.the clan itself was historically very integrated into kine society so it's not like they were bad at being a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-18-2021, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T16:15:27-07:00","id":1460383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460317#post1460317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a child now need 5 dots to use Mortis? Does a sire have time to teach them that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Five dots in an ability represents the maximum human potential in a lifetime of dedicated study. Otherwise known as, more or less, the amount of time a vampire in the Dark Ages spends with their sire prior to being released...<i>not accounting for what the fledgling learned when they were still mortal</i>. So...yes?<br /> <br /> It's funny this only seems to be an issue when it comes to Cappadocians, really. It doesn't seem to be an issue with any other clan that specializes in a given ability set, whether it's martially-inclined Brujah, Ventrue in the ways of leadership and politics, Tremere and the occult, Toreador with history and art, Gangrel with &quot;mere&quot; survival...alas, for some incomprehensible reason, it's only the <i>Cappadocians</i> who apparently struggle with honing a childe's skillset upon which they will rely in unlife to a fine point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fortitude is not a great hunting discipline<br /> Auspex is not a great hunting discipline. </div> </div> </div>Only in <i>your</i> mind, because your mind seems constrained to the concept of feeding as exclusively &quot;go out, seduce mortal or bonk them on head, have a sip&quot;. Literally no one else in this thread struggles with this (fundamentally simple) concept; perhaps <i>you're</i> the problematic element, here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Morits apparently requires massive amounts of pre-modern medical knowledge. So either the sire needs to invest a lot of time into a knowledge (in addition to teaching them the rules and regulations of undead society, how to feed without getting caught and so on) or the sire can embrace some of the very few medical experts to save themselves a lot of time. </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it does. And yet, you seem to struggle with the idea of how that skillset can be employed for the precise purpose of feeding, when it's been spelled out for you, step by step, in exact, simple language.<br /> <br /> In a historical game setting in which the predominant medical treatment was <i><u><b>bloodletting</b></u></i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neither option looks great if you want Capadocians to be a big, thriving bloodline on par with any of the big six. And you still haven't adressed how the more Capadocians there are, the less valuable their services. </div> </div> </div>And you don't seem to have noted the utterance of the word &quot;cartel&quot;, or understand what it means. Which is ironic, considering how great a game you're talking up the <i>Giovanni</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-18-2021, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T08:09:33-07:00","id":1464383,"title":"","content":"I have said this before, but, of all the clans the Tzimisce are unfairly pigeonholed the most. And what's weird is that it's always as the Old Clan landed gentry even tho that part of the clan has been a tiny minority literally ever since the Anarch Revolt. The Old Can are to the Tzimisce what the True Brujah are to the regular Brujah. They are a Dark Ages hold out that do not fit in Modern Nights. The Tzimisce are a clan that's defined by embracing change and evolution, thats how you end up with characters like Vykos and Rattie-Ben and why they started the Anarch Revolt and why in V5 they have joined the Movement propper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T10:30:28-07:00","id":1464391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460085#post1460085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By portraying the Sabbat the way it does, VtM delves in the practice of portraying their chosen cities as cesspools of unimaginable violence where nothing makes sense. Because no, they're not portrayed as sensible monsters that at least know how to keep the masquerade, they're portrayed as unstoppable lunatics engaging in their antics with full supernatural might every night, raging across the streets in plain sight.<br /> <br /> What does that tell you about the places they live in? And which places were chosen for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, cesspools of unimaginable violence, such as Scandinavia. As per <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat,</i> the entirety of my country, Finland, is Sabbat territory. I'm sure we're all eager to hear about the supposed anti-Finnish slant of the original Sabbat writers, since you're implying that their antipathy toward Latin America is the reason for the Sabbat's presence there.<br /> <br /> Or maybe your ridiculous caricature of the 2nd Edition Sabbat is just that, a ridiculous caricature that does not reflect the original texts nor the authors' attitudes about real-world populations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1460021#post1460021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making the Sabbat really be the whimsical bloodfest it was rumored to be and at the same time a political powerhouse was one of the stupidest ideas ever, the clans developed for it didn't made sense, and then a lot of effort was put in the following years to create reason out of this mess without outwardly assuming it was stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me quote your own words from another thread right back at you: <i>&quot;You don't like when people crap on your favorite play style and faction, don't do that on others. It doesn't help your cause.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T20:46:22-07:00","id":1464683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1464391#post1464391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure we're all eager to hear about the supposed anti-Finnish slant of the original Sabbat writers, since you're implying that their antipathy toward Latin America is the reason for the Sabbat's presence there.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm not implying that. I'm outward saying that the depiction of the Sabbat as the all-caps EVIL 24/7 violence orgy in the streets is an offensive take on the cities where it would be occurring as it not only describes those places as &quot;Mordor&quot;, as some termed it in other threads, but implies they're too &quot;uncivilized&quot; for this to break the Masquerade, which either means the people is incapable of recognizing the supernatural, have not enough grasp of modern civilization to count for that, have no impact on public knowledge, or a combination of those.<br /> <br /> So, first, it is against one depiction and not every representation of the Sabbat. Second I don't think they have to actively dislike something to make wrong assumptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1464391#post1464391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe your ridiculous caricature of the 2nd Edition Sabbat is just that, a ridiculous caricature that does not reflect the original texts nor the authors' attitudes about real-world populations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe my ridiculous caricature is a take on the sect that I don't like because it is a ridiculous caricature that, taken at face value, offends me. Observing that what I don't like is the caricature itself, not the Sabbat as a whole.<br /> <br /> And sometimes I may write thinking back on the past, in a time when I indeed believed the sect to be that ridiculous caricature, a time when I in fact didn't like the Sabbat, and if I expressed myself poorly because of that I do apologize, as was the case here because I was answering a comment by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, that actually enjoys the caricature.<br /> <br /> So just to remind you, ridiculous as it may seen this caricature is the Sabbat that many players know about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1464391#post1464391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, yes, cesspools of unimaginable violence, such as Scandinavia. As per <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat,</i> the entirety of my country, Finland, is Sabbat territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I totally forgot to check with a white person if my feelings are valid in polite society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458511-tzimisce-rule-the-camarilla?p=1464391#post1464391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me quote your own words from another thread right back at you</div> </div> </div> </div>You are partially right. To comment about a caricature I forgot to state it was just one possible take on it, and that it could be done in many different ways. Although I didn't at any point said that it was wrong as a playstyle, even if that portrait is taken at face value. I did had fun playing Sabbat before and I still have STing Sabbat games.<br /> <br /> Just let me add that in my opinion there is a huge difference between saying <i>&quot;describing my region as being dominated by this sect feels offensive&quot;</i> and saying <i>&quot;this is just a crappy excuse for a sect.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}